{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SQz23bG5qeWP58JFATxqAP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '2-axis framework directionally correct but需要 qualify 2-3 个 edge\n2\t  cases。 Claim 1 弱化为 ''primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity\n3\t  as a modulating factor''。 Claim 5 加限定 ''at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)''，k=0.3\n4\t  reversal 移入 Discussion。 VTR 明确为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。Paper identity 从\n5\t  ''analysis + method'' 调整为 ''primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case\n6\t  architecture''。 Title 改为更保守的 ''How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness\n7\t  in VLAs''。 仍提交 CoRL，contribution statement 聚焦 diagnostic insight。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: π0.5 4-Suite Pruning Characterization — Median Tier Consolidation\n12\t  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n13\t  description: 'π0.5 (4B, PaliGemma linear proj, CV=0.055) 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 的 pruning\n14\t    response。 Median tier 预测：Object 上 random cliff (k=0.85-0.925) 是 Object-specific\n15\t    而非 universal； Goal/Long 上 Axis-2 amplification 弱于 X-VLA (<15pp for π0.5 vs 27.8pp\n16\t    for X-VLA)。 CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论。\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    pi05_baseline_object: 98.2\n21\t    pi05_baseline_spatial: 97.2\n22\t    pi05_baseline_goal: 96.4\n23\t    pi05_baseline_long: 92.8\n24\t    pi05_cv: 0.055\n25\t    pi05_random_k095_object_sr: 72.5\n26\t    pi05_random_k0925_object_sr: 28.8\n27\t    pi05_random_k09_object_sr: 10.2\n28\t    pi05_random_k085_object_sr: 4.4\n29\t    pi05_random_k07_object_sr: 75.5\n30\t    pi05_random_k05_object_sr: 68.9\n31\t    pi05_random_k03_object_sr: 34.3\n32\t    pi05_l2norm_k095_object_sr: 98.2\n33\t    pi05_l2norm_k0925_object_sr: 99.2\n34\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr: 98.2\n35\t    pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr: 98.0\n36\t    pi05_l2norm_k07_object_sr: 56.4\n37\t    pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr: 33.5\n38\t    pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr: 53.2\n39\t    pi05_random_k095_spatial_sr: 76.6\n40\t    pi05_random_k0925_spatial_sr: 59.3\n41\t    pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr: 54.0\n42\t    pi05_random_k085_spatial_sr: 58.8\n43\t    pi05_random_k07_spatial_sr: 74.1\n44\t    pi05_random_k05_spatial_sr: 72.0\n45\t    pi05_random_k03_spatial_sr: 48.4\n46\t    pi05_l2norm_k095_spatial_sr: 97.9\n47\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr: 95.3\n48\t    pi05_l2norm_k085_spatial_sr: 88.8\n49\t    pi05_l2norm_k07_spatial_sr: 67.7\n50\t    pi05_l2norm_k05_spatial_sr: 55.7\n51\t    pi05_l2norm_k03_spatial_sr: 55.0\n52\t    pi05_random_k095_goal_sr: 83.5\n53\t    pi05_random_k09_goal_sr: 61.7\n54\t    pi05_random_k085_goal_sr: 52.6\n55\t    pi05_random_k07_goal_sr: 76.9\n56\t    pi05_random_k05_goal_sr: 73.6\n57\t    pi05_random_k03_goal_sr: 51.7\n58\t    pi05_l2norm_k095_goal_sr: 90.1\n59\t    pi05_l2norm_k0925_goal_sr: 89.6\n60\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr: 89.8\n61\t    pi05_l2norm_k085_goal_sr: 87.5\n62\t    pi05_l2norm_k07_goal_sr: 72.0\n63\t    pi05_l2norm_k05_goal_sr: 59.5\n64\t    pi05_l2norm_k03_goal_sr: 51.8\n65\t    pi05_random_k095_long_sr: 62.2\n66\t    pi05_random_k09_long_sr: 31.3\n67\t    pi05_random_k085_long_sr: 44.3\n68\t    pi05_random_k07_long_sr: 66.3\n69\t    pi05_random_k05_long_sr: 47.6\n70\t    pi05_random_k03_long_sr: 28.7\n71\t    pi05_l2norm_k095_long_sr: 87.2\n72\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr: 80.3\n73\t    pi05_l2norm_k085_long_sr: 78.8\n74\t    pi05_l2norm_k07_long_sr: 63.5\n75\t    pi05_l2norm_k05_long_sr: 51.4\n76\t    pi05_l2norm_k03_long_sr: 37.5\n77\t    axis2_amplification_object_pp: 88.0\n78\t    axis2_amplification_spatial_pp: 43.2\n79\t    axis2_amplification_goal_pp: 34.7\n80\t    axis2_amplification_long_pp: 61.5\n81\t    pi05_axis2_object_vs_goal_random_k09_pp: -51.5\n82\t    pi05_axis2_object_vs_spatial_random_k09_pp: -43.8\n83\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_object_pp: -35.4\n84\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spatial_pp: -16.3\n85\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_goal_pp: -14.1\n86\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_long_pp: 3.8\n87\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_object_pp: 18.9\n88\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spatial_pp: 6.6\n89\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_goal_pp: 0.1\n90\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_long_pp: 8.8\n91\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 下 π0.5 数据呈现三个关键 pattern：\n92\t\n93\t    (1) Random cliff 是 Object-specific。Object suite 在 k=0.85-0.925 出现灾难性 dip (5%→10.8%→27.6%)，但\n94\t    Spatial 的 floor 保持在 54% 以上，Goal 在 k=0.9 仍有 61.7%。 这是因为 Object 任务需要精确的 object identity\n95\t    discrimination（视觉相似物体间区分）， 而 random 在 cliff zone 恰好破坏了 concentrated critical tokens。Spatial\n96\t    的关键信息 是分布式的（layout patches），Goal 的关键信息由 language 部分承载。\n97\t\n98\t    (2) Axis-2 amplification 对 π0.5 表现为 REVERSED pattern：Goal 和 Spatial 在 k=0.9 random\n99\t    下反而 BETTER than Object（61.7% vs 10.2%）。这与 X-VLA 的 pattern 完全相反 （X-VLA Goal k=0.9\n100\t    比 Object 差 27.8pp）。原因：token-independent connector 下， pruning damage 是 local 的，不会\n101\t    cascade。Object 的 cliff 是 random sampling 的 统计效应（concentrated critical tokens），不是\n102\t    task complexity amplification。 因此 median tier 预测 π0.5 的 Axis-2 amplification <15pp（如果排除\n103\t    Object cliff zone）， 需要在 paper 中 qualify 2-axis framework 对 token-independent connector\n104\t    的适用性。\n105\t\n106\t    (3) CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立：L2norm-random gap = -35.4pp（Object），与 CV=0.055 的极低值一致。但\n107\t    k=0.3 出现 reversal：L2norm 反而 +18.9pp 领先。这是因为 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（足够大的 budget），L2norm\n108\t    的 spatial clustering 在此 budget 下 反而 fragment 成多个 cluster，恢复了 spatial coverage。k=0.5\n109\t    是 clustering 最严重的 sweet spot（1 cluster, 100% concentration, 78% coverage）。\n110\t\n111\t    '\n112\t  tables:\n113\t  - caption: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random Pruning — Cliff Zone Comparison\n114\t    columns:\n115\t    - Suite\n116\t    - k=0.95\n117\t    - k=0.925\n118\t    - k=0.9\n119\t    - k=0.85\n120\t    - k=0.7\n121\t    - k=0.5\n122\t    - k=0.3\n123\t    rows:\n124\t    - - Object\n125\t      - 72.5%\n126\t      - 28.8%\n127\t      - 10.2%\n128\t      - 4.4%\n129\t      - 75.5%\n130\t      - 68.9%\n131\t      - 34.3%\n132\t    - - Spatial\n133\t      - 76.6%\n134\t      - 59.3%\n135\t      - 54.0%\n136\t      - 58.8%\n137\t      - 74.1%\n138\t      - 72.0%\n139\t      - 48.4%\n140\t    - - Goal\n141\t      - 83.5%\n142\t      - —\n143\t      - 61.7%\n144\t      - 52.6%\n145\t      - 76.9%\n146\t      - 73.6%\n147\t      - 51.7%\n148\t    - - Long\n149\t      - 62.2%\n150\t      - —\n151\t      - 31.3%\n152\t      - 44.3%\n153\t      - 66.3%\n154\t      - 47.6%\n155\t      - 28.7%\n156\t  - caption: π0.5 L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) — CV Scaling Law Validation\n157\t    columns:\n158\t    - Suite\n159\t    - k=0.7\n160\t    - k=0.5\n161\t    - k=0.3\n162\t    - Pattern\n163\t    rows:\n164\t    - - Object\n165\t      - '-19.1'\n166\t      - '-35.4'\n167\t      - '+18.9'\n168\t      - Reversal at k=0.3\n169\t    - - Spatial\n170\t      - '-6.4'\n171\t      - '-16.3'\n172\t      - '+6.6'\n173\t      - Reversal at k=0.3\n174\t    - - Goal\n175\t      - '-4.9'\n176\t      - '-14.1'\n177\t      - '+0.1'\n178\t      - Near-zero at k=0.3\n179\t    - - Long\n180\t      - '-2.8'\n181\t      - '+3.8'\n182\t      - '+8.8'\n183\t      - L2norm consistently better\n184\t  figures_description:\n185\t  - 'Fig: π0.5 random pruning cliff profile — Object (deep V-shape dip to 4.4% at\n186\t    k=0.85) vs Spatial (gradual, floor >54%) vs Goal/Long. Key visual: Object-specific\n187\t    catastrophic collapse.'\n188\t  - 'Fig: L2norm-Random gap vs keep ratio across 4 suites — showing k=0.5 as peak\n189\t    random advantage and k=0.3 reversal point.'\n190\t  analysis: 'Median tier 下需要在 paper 中加 qualification：2-axis framework 的 Axis-2 (task\n191\t    complexity) 对 token-independent connector 的 amplification effect 显著弱于 token-entangling\n192\t    connector。 π0.5 的 suite-dependent sensitivity 主要由 Object cliff（random sampling\n193\t    + concentrated critical tokens 的统计效应）驱动，而非 task complexity amplification。 Claim\n194\t    1 需弱化为 ''connector architecture is the primary determinant; task complexity is\n195\t    a modulating factor primarily for token-entangling connectors''。 CV scaling law\n196\t    (Claim 5) 在 k=0.5 清晰成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论—— Long suite 在所有 k 值 L2norm 都不差于\n197\t    random，可能是 Long 任务的 multi-step 结构 使得 importance-based selection 的 token 恰好 cover\n198\t    关键 subgoal transitions。\n199\t\n200\t    '\n201\t- name: Cross-Suite Framework Validation — 5 Models × 4 Suites\n202\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n203\t  description: '将 pruning 实验从 LIBERO-Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。 验证 2-axis framework\n204\t    跨 suite 的预测准确性。 Median tier 预测 framework accuracy 75-90%。\n205\t\n206\t    '\n207\t  expected_results:\n208\t    xvla_baseline_object: 99.2\n209\t    xvla_baseline_spatial: 93.0\n210\t    xvla_baseline_goal: 98.4\n211\t    xvla_baseline_long: 94.0\n212\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_object: 97.6\n213\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial: 78.8\n214\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_goal: 70.2\n215\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_long: 27.5\n216\t    xvla_random_k09_object: 97.8\n217\t    xvla_random_k09_spatial: 77.8\n218\t    xvla_random_k09_goal: 70.6\n219\t    xvla_random_k09_long: 29.6\n220\t    xvla_drop_k09_object_pp: 1.6\n221\t    xvla_drop_k09_spatial_pp: 14.2\n222\t    xvla_drop_k09_goal_pp: 28.2\n223\t    xvla_drop_k09_long_pp: 66.5\n224\t    xvla_l2norm_k05_object: 43.4\n225\t    xvla_random_k05_object: 70.3\n226\t    xvla_l2norm_k05_spatial: 58.9\n227\t    xvla_random_k05_spatial: 71.4\n228\t    xvla_l2norm_k05_goal: 59.5\n229\t    xvla_random_k05_goal: 67.9\n230\t    xvla_l2norm_k05_long: 44.8\n231\t    xvla_random_k05_long: 61.6\n232\t    smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n233\t    smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n234\t    smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n235\t    smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n236\t    smolvla_k095_all_suites_all_methods: 0\n237\t    framework_correct_predictions: 17\n238\t    framework_total_predictions: 20\n239\t    framework_accuracy_pct: 85\n240\t    edge_case_1: π0.5 Axis-2 reversed — Goal BETTER than Object at k=0.9\n241\t    edge_case_2: X-VLA Long k=0.85 non-monotonic (35%) < k=0.5 (61.6%)\n242\t    edge_case_3: CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models\n243\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier framework accuracy ~85%：20 个 cross-suite predictions\n244\t    中 17 个正确。\n245\t\n246\t    正确的 predictions： - X-VLA Axis-2 amplification Object→Goal/Long（confirmed 27.8pp/66.5pp）\n247\t    - SmolVLA all suites cliff-edge（confirmed 0% everywhere） - OpenVLA graded degradation\n248\t    across suites - CV scaling law at k=0.5（L2norm-random gap correlates with CV）\n249\t    - L2norm plateau for π0.5 at k≥0.85 on all suites\n250\t\n251\t    需要 qualify 的 edge cases： (1) π0.5 的 Axis-2 pattern 是 reversed（Object WORST, not\n252\t    Goal/Long），因为 token-independent connector 下 task complexity 不 amplify damage，而\n253\t    Object 的 concentrated critical tokens 在 random cliff zone 反而最脆弱。 (2) X-VLA Long\n254\t    k=0.85 出现 non-monotonic reversal（35% < k=0.5 的 61.6%）， 与 Object 的 non-monotonic\n255\t    pattern 不同——Long 的 cliff zone 在更高 k 值， 因为 multi-step reasoning 对 token density\n256\t    的 threshold 更高。 (3) CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal 限制了 Claim 5 的适用范围。\n257\t\n258\t    '\n259\t  tables:\n260\t  - caption: 2-Axis Framework — X-VLA Pruning Drop at k=0.9 Across Suites\n261\t    columns:\n262\t    - Suite\n263\t    - Baseline\n264\t    - L2norm k=0.9\n265\t    - Drop (pp)\n266\t    - Axis-2 Level\n267\t    rows:\n268\t    - - Object\n269\t      - 99.2%\n270\t      - 97.6%\n271\t      - '-1.6'\n272\t      - Simple\n273\t    - - Spatial\n274\t      - 93.0%\n275\t      - 78.8%\n276\t      - '-14.2'\n277\t      - Moderate\n278\t    - - Goal\n279\t      - 98.4%\n280\t      - 70.2%\n281\t      - '-28.2'\n282\t      - Complex\n283\t    - - Long\n284\t      - 94.0%\n285\t      - 27.5%\n286\t      - '-66.5'\n287\t      - Most Complex\n288\t  - caption: Cross-Suite L2norm vs Random Gap at k=0.5 (pp) — CV Scaling Law\n289\t    columns:\n290\t    - Model\n291\t    - CV\n292\t    - Object\n293\t    - Spatial\n294\t    - Goal\n295\t    - Long\n296\t    rows:\n297\t    - - pi0.5\n298\t      - '0.055'\n299\t      - '-35.4'\n300\t      - '-16.3'\n301\t      - '-14.1'\n302\t      - '+3.8'\n303\t    - - X-VLA\n304\t      - '0.151'\n305\t      - '-26.9'\n306\t      - '-12.5'\n307\t      - '-8.4'\n308\t      - '-16.8'\n309\t    - - OpenVLA\n310\t      - '0.215'\n311\t      - '+1.8'\n312\t      - —\n313\t      - —\n314\t      - —\n315\t  figures_description:\n316\t  - 'Fig: Heatmap of pruning drop (pp from baseline) — 5 models × 4 suites × k=0.9.\n317\t    Visual shows clear Axis-1 (rows) and Axis-2 (columns) gradients for X-VLA/SmolVLA,\n318\t    but flat for π0.5/OpenVLA across suites.'\n319\t  analysis: 'Framework accuracy 85% 落在 median tier range [75%, 90%] 中。3 个 edge cases\n320\t    需要在 paper 中 qualify：(1) 对 π0.5 等 token-independent model，用 ''connector architecture\n321\t    determines base sensitivity; task semantics modulate through statistical token\n322\t    criticality rather than cascading damage'' 替代原先的 ''task complexity amplifies''。\n323\t    (2) X-VLA Long 的 non-monotonic pattern 需要额外 figure 说明 cliff zone 随 task complexity\n324\t    右移。(3) k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion 中说明 CV scaling law 的边界条件。\n325\t\n326\t    '\n327\t- name: VTR SmolVLA Cross-Suite Recovery (M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\n328\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n329\t  description: 'VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long 上的 recovery 验证。 已有数据：M=32 Spatial=53.2%,\n330\t    Goal=56.4%。 Median tier 预测 recovery ratio 0.9-1.0。\n331\t\n332\t    '\n333\t  expected_results:\n334\t    smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n335\t    smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n336\t    smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n337\t    smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n338\t    smolvla_prune_k05_all_suites: 0\n339\t    vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1\n340\t    vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2\n341\t    vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4\n342\t    vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.0\n343\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n344\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n345\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n346\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_long: 0.956\n347\t    vtr_mean_recovery_ratio: 0.96\n348\t    vtr_m16_object_sr: 56.9\n349\t    vtr_m32_object_sr_confirmed: 60.1\n350\t    vtr_m64_object_sr: 62.0\n351\t    vtr_m96_object_sr: 54.5\n352\t    vtr_m128_object_sr: 58.0\n353\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 下 VTR 在所有 suites 都能从 0%（hard pruning）恢复到 near-baseline，\n354\t    但 recovery ratio 有 suite-dependent variation（0.928-1.193）。\n355\t\n356\t    Object (recovery 1.015): VTR 在 Object 上 recovery 最稳定，因为 Object 任务的 visual discriminability\n357\t    需求可以被 re-encoded tokens 完整保留——pixel-shuffle 的 spatial entanglement 是 Object failure\n358\t    的唯一原因，VTR 修复了这个 entanglement。\n359\t\n360\t    Spatial (recovery 1.193): 看似超过 baseline 但需注意 baseline 是 official checkpoint (44.6%)\n361\t    vs VTR 是 LoRA-FT + VTC (53.2%)——实际上是不同 training pipeline 的差异， 不应解读为 VTR 超越。Paper\n362\t    中需要用 recovery from 0% 而非 absolute comparison。\n363\t\n364\t    Goal (recovery 0.928): 轻微低于 baseline（-4.4pp），因为 VTR 是在 Object suite 训练的， Goal\n365\t    的 multi-step task structure 引入了 distribution shift。Token re-encoding 恢复了 spatial\n366\t    information 但无法完全补偿 task-distribution mismatch。\n367\t\n368\t    Long (predicted 0.956): Long 的 baseline 最低（36.6%），VTR 的 re-encoding 在 simple manipulation\n369\t    primitives 上有效，但 Long 需要跨多个 sub-goal 的 temporal coherence， VTR 的 per-step re-encoding\n370\t    无法显式捕捉 cross-step dependencies。预测 recovery ~35%， 略低于 baseline 但远高于 0%。\n371\t\n372\t    关键限定：VTR 仅对 pixel-shuffle connector 有效（OpenVLA M=128 = 0%），method contribution\n373\t    限于 ''targeted solution for worst-case architecture''。\n374\t\n375\t    '\n376\t  tables:\n377\t  - caption: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery from Cliff-Edge\n378\t    columns:\n379\t    - Suite\n380\t    - Baseline\n381\t    - Hard Prune k=0.5\n382\t    - VTR M=32\n383\t    - Recovery Ratio\n384\t    rows:\n385\t    - - Object\n386\t      - 59.2%\n387\t      - 0%\n388\t      - 60.1%\n389\t      - '1.015'\n390\t    - - Spatial\n391\t      - 44.6%*\n392\t      - 0%\n393\t      - 53.2%\n394\t      - 1.193*\n395\t    - - Goal\n396\t      - 60.8%\n397\t      - 0%\n398\t      - 56.4%\n399\t      - '0.928'\n400\t    - - Long\n401\t      - 36.6%\n402\t      - 0%\n403\t      - ~35.0%\n404\t      - ~0.956\n405\t  figures_description:\n406\t  - 'Fig: Bar chart — SmolVLA Baseline vs Hard Prune vs VTR M=32 across 4 suites.\n407\t    Visual emphasis on recovery from 0% (red) to near-baseline (green).'\n408\t  analysis: 'VTR 的 mean recovery ratio 0.96 落在 median tier range [0.9, 1.0] 中。 Method\n409\t    contribution 需明确限定为 pixel-shuffle-specific：(1) 只在 SmolVLA 上有效， (2) 在非 Object suite\n410\t    上有 -4.4pp 到 +8.6pp 的 variance，(3) OpenVLA VTR = 0%。 Paper identity 从 ''analysis\n411\t    + method'' 调整为 ''primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case architecture''。\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t- name: VTR/VTC on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — Universality Falsification\n415\t  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n416\t  description: 'VTR M=128 已确认 0% SR（overfitting）。VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress。\n417\t    Median tier 预测 VTC-only 也失败，VTR 限于 pixel-shuffle。\n418\t\n419\t    '\n420\t  expected_results:\n421\t    openvla_vtr_m128_20k_sr: 0\n422\t    openvla_baseline_object_sr: 74\n423\t    openvla_vtc_m32_sr: 0\n424\t    openvla_vtc_m64_sr: 0\n425\t    openvla_vtc_m96_sr: 0\n426\t    openvla_vtc_m32_train_loss: 2.5\n427\t    openvla_vtc_m64_train_loss: 2.4\n428\t    openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n429\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 预测 VTC-only M=32/M=64 也会失败，原因是 MLP projector tokens\n430\t    已经是 individually meaningful 的——re-encoding 增加了不必要的 bottleneck，导致 overfitting。\n431\t\n432\t    具体机制：OpenVLA 的 3-layer MLP connector 将 SigLIP features 映射为 256 个独立的 vision tokens，每个\n433\t    token 保留了原始 spatial meaning。VTR/VTC 在这些 tokens 上 添加 cross-attention / MLP adapter\n434\t    作为 bottleneck，但这些 tokens 不需要 ''re-encoding''——它们的 spatial information 没有被 entangle。额外的\n435\t    bottleneck 反而限制了 information flow，导致模型 overfit 到 training set 的 action distribution。\n436\t\n437\t    实际 training logs 显示 M=128 在 20K steps 后 output 是 identical action（所有 observation\n438\t    产生相同的 action sequence），这是 severe mode collapse 的 hallmark。 M=32/M=64 的更强 compression\n439\t    会加剧而非缓解这个问题。\n440\t\n441\t    Training 失败的 root cause 也可能是 OpenVLA 的 7B model size 导致 VTC 的 22M params 相对过小（0.3%\n442\t    of model）——gradient signal 在 backprop 过程中被 diluted。\n443\t\n444\t    这个 negative result 反而 strengthens 论文：VTR 的有效性是 connector-dependent 的， 验证了 ''connector\n445\t    determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy''。\n446\t\n447\t    '\n448\t  tables:\n449\t  - caption: VTR/VTC on OpenVLA vs SmolVLA — Connector-Dependent Effectiveness\n450\t    columns:\n451\t    - Model\n452\t    - Connector\n453\t    - CV\n454\t    - VTR M=128\n455\t    - VTC M=32\n456\t    - VTC M=64\n457\t    rows:\n458\t    - - SmolVLA\n459\t      - Pixel-shuffle\n460\t      - '0.314'\n461\t      - 58.0%\n462\t      - 60.1%\n463\t      - 62.0%\n464\t    - - OpenVLA\n465\t      - 3-layer MLP\n466\t      - '0.215'\n467\t      - 0%\n468\t      - ~0%*\n469\t      - ~0%*\n470\t  figures_description:\n471\t  - 'Fig: Training loss curves — SmolVLA VTC (converges to ~0.05) vs OpenVLA VTC (plateaus\n472\t    at ~2.5, fails to converge). Annotate divergence point.'\n473\t  analysis: 'VTR universality falsified。Method contribution 收窄为 pixel-shuffle-specific\n474\t    solution。 Paper 中将 VTR 定位为 ''targeted re-encoding for architectures where token\n475\t    pruning creates irreversible information loss''。Discussion 中指出 MLP projector VLAs\n476\t    应 直接用 simple pruning（L2norm 或 random depending on CV），不需要 learned compression。\n477\t\n478\t    '\n479\t- name: OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96) — Training Convergence Test\n480\t  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n481\t  description: 'OpenVLA 上 VTC-only training（不冻结 backbone），测试不同 M 值。 Training 已 failed/killed\n482\t    on all M values。\n483\t\n484\t    '\n485\t  expected_results:\n486\t    openvla_vtc_m32_status: failed\n487\t    openvla_vtc_m64_status: failed\n488\t    openvla_vtc_m96_status: failed\n489\t    openvla_vtc_m96_final_loss: 2.45\n490\t    openvla_vtc_m64_final_loss: null\n491\t    interpretation: VTC training does not converge on MLP-projector VLAs\n492\t  result_rationale: 'All M values 的 VTC training 在 OpenVLA 上失败或 killed。M=96 跑完了 100K\n493\t    steps 但 final loss 2.45（远高于 SmolVLA 的 ~0.05），说明模型未能学到有效的 token re-encoding。M=64\n494\t    和 M=32 的 VTC-only training 也 crashed/failed。\n495\t\n496\t    Root cause：OpenVLA (7B) 是 frozen backbone + 22M compressor 的极端不平衡。 SmolVLA (450M)\n497\t    的 compressor/backbone ratio = 22M/450M = 4.9%，而 OpenVLA 的 ratio = 22M/7B = 0.3%。VTC\n498\t    的 gradient signal 在通过 7B frozen backbone 的 attention layers 时被严重 attenuate，导致\n499\t    compressor 无法学到有用的 representation。\n500\t\n501\t    '\n502\t  tables: []\n503\t  figures_description: []\n504\t  analysis: 'OpenVLA VTC M-sweep 的 universal failure 进一步确认 VTR/VTC 仅对 pixel-shuffle\n505\t    connector 有效。Paper 中在 Table 5 或 supplementary 中报告这些 negative results， 强化 ''VTR\n506\t    effectiveness is connector-dependent'' 的 claim。\n507\t\n508\t    '\n509\t- name: OpenVLA-OFT Cross-Suite Pruning (Blocked by GPU Incompatibility)\n510\t  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n511\t  description: 'OFT (7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fused, 512 tokens) 在 4 suites\n512\t    上的 baseline + pruning。Blocked by Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility。 Median tier\n513\t    用 CV/entropy analysis 替代 SR eval。\n514\t\n515\t    '\n516\t  expected_results:\n517\t    oft_cv: 0.219\n518\t    oft_entropy: 0.667\n519\t    oft_tokens: 512\n520\t    oft_baseline_official_sr: 97\n521\t    oft_predicted_k09_sr: 65\n522\t    oft_predicted_k07_sr: 50\n523\t    oft_predicted_k05_sr: 38\n524\t    oft_predicted_k03_sr: 22\n525\t    oft_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp: -2\n526\t    oft_l2norm_advantage_mild_k: true\n527\t    blocker: Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility — requires A100 + torch 2.2\n528\t  result_rationale: 'OFT eval 被 Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA 不兼容 blocked。Median tier 下仅用 diagnostic\n529\t    metrics 参与分析：CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA (0.215)，entropy=0.667 ≈ OpenVLA (0.661)。\n530\t\n531\t    这两个 near-identical diagnostic values 预测 OFT 的 pruning behavior 与 OpenVLA 几乎一致——graded\n532\t    degradation，L2norm 在 aggressive k 略优于 random。 512 tokens (vs OpenVLA 的 256) 意味着\n533\t    absolute token budget 在 same k ratio 下 更大（k=0.5 保留 256 vs 128），可能导致略好的 SR，但 degradation\n534\t    PATTERN 应相同。\n535\t\n536\t    关键 paper value：OFT 用了不同的 action head（Optimal Flow Transport vs standard）， 但 CV\n537\t    和 entropy 几乎 identical → 确认 connector（not action head）determines attention structure\n538\t    和 pruning behavior。这是一个 clean controlled comparison。\n539\t\n540\t    Median tier 下 OFT 作为 supplementary evidence 出现（CV/entropy table）， 不作为 primary\n541\t    experimental evidence。Cite official baseline ~97%， acknowledge eval 未能完成。\n542\t\n543\t    '\n544\t  tables:\n545\t  - caption: Connector vs Action Head — Diagnostic Decoupling\n546\t    columns:\n547\t    - Model\n548\t    - Action Head\n549\t    - Connector\n550\t    - CV\n551\t    - Entropy\n552\t    rows:\n553\t    - - OpenVLA\n554\t      - Standard (MLP)\n555\t      - 3-layer MLP\n556\t      - '0.215'\n557\t      - '0.661'\n558\t    - - OpenVLA-OFT\n559\t      - OFT (flow)\n560\t      - 3-layer MLP\n561\t      - '0.219'\n562\t      - '0.667'\n563\t  figures_description:\n564\t  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of CV vs Entropy for all 6 models — OFT and OpenVLA as overlapping\n565\t    points, confirming connector-dominance over action-head.'\n566\t  analysis: 'OFT 贡献收窄为 diagnostic decoupling evidence。Paper 中用一句话总结： ''OFT (CV=0.219)\n567\t    ≈ Standard OpenVLA (CV=0.215) despite different action heads, confirming that\n568\t    connector architecture, not downstream components, determines token importance\n569\t    distribution.'' Eval SR 不可得，acknowledged as limitation。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t- name: OFT Token Importance CV Measurement\n573\t  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n574\t  description: 'OFT importance CV 测量，完成 6-model diagnostic table 的最后一个空位。\n575\t\n576\t    '\n577\t  expected_results:\n578\t    oft_importance_cv: 0.219\n579\t    oft_importance_cv_std: 0.012\n580\t    oft_importance_gini: 0.11\n581\t    oft_n_tokens: 512\n582\t    spectrum_position: between OpenVLA (0.215) and SmolVLA (0.314)\n583\t  result_rationale: 'OFT 使用与 OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector（GELU activation），唯一差异是\n584\t    (1) fused DINOv2+SigLIP encoder 产生 512 tokens（vs OpenVLA 的 256）， (2) OFT action\n585\t    head。Entropy 已确认 0.667 ≈ 0.661，CV 预测 0.219 ≈ 0.215。 微小的 CV 差异（+0.004）可能来自 DINOv2\n586\t    features 的 additional modality 引入的 slightly higher token heterogeneity。\n587\t\n588\t    '\n589\t  tables: []\n590\t  figures_description: []\n591\t  analysis: 'CV=0.219 完成 6-model spectrum：π0(0.038) < π0.5(0.055) < X-VLA(0.151) <\n592\t    OpenVLA(0.215) ≈ OFT(0.219) < SmolVLA(0.314)。 Paper Table 1 中 OFT 行填入 CV=0.219,\n593\t    Entropy=0.667, Pruning=''Graded (predicted)''。\n594\t\n595\t    '\n596\t- name: X-VLA k=0.8/k=0.85 3-Seed Cliff Localization\n597\t  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n598\t  description: 'X-VLA Object cliff threshold 精确定位：k=0.85 (67.9% ± 0.31pp, 3-seed)\n599\t    和 k=0.80 (89.0% ± 0.72pp, 3-seed)。Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80。\n600\t\n601\t    '\n602\t  expected_results:\n603\t    xvla_l2norm_k085_object_mean: 67.9\n604\t    xvla_l2norm_k085_object_std: 0.31\n605\t    xvla_l2norm_k085_seeds:\n606\t    - 68.0\n607\t    - 67.6\n608\t    - 68.2\n609\t    xvla_l2norm_k080_object_mean: 89.0\n610\t    xvla_l2norm_k080_object_std: 0.72\n611\t    xvla_l2norm_k080_seeds:\n612\t    - 88.8\n613\t    - 88.4\n614\t    - 89.8\n615\t    xvla_random_k085_object_mean: 64.3\n616\t    xvla_random_k085_seeds:\n617\t    - 65.0\n618\t    - 63.6\n619\t    - 63.2\n620\t    xvla_random_k080_object_mean: 89.4\n621\t    xvla_random_k080_seeds:\n622\t    - 89.4\n623\t    non_monotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n624\t    cliff_width_k_units: 0.05\n625\t    l2norm_random_k085_gap_pp: 3.6\n626\t    both_crash_same_tasks: true\n627\t  result_rationale: \"3-seed deterministic data 确认 cliff 位于 k=0.85（42 tokens kept），且\\\n628\t    \\ k=0.80（40 tokens）recovery 到 89%——仅差 2 个 tokens 但 21pp gap。\\nNon-monotonicity\\\n629\t    \\ 来自 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interactions： - k=0.85 (42 tokens): BART\\\n630\t    \\ 的 12-layer self-attention 在 42 tokens 上产生\\n  destructive interference pattern——刚好是\\\n631\t    \\ critical token density threshold\\n- k=0.80 (40 tokens): 少保留 2 个 tokens 反而破坏了这个\\\n632\t    \\ interference pattern，\\n  恢复了正常的 information flow\\n\\nSD < 1pp across all 3 seeds\\\n633\t    \\ 确认 cliff 是完全 deterministic 的（L2norm pruning 是 deterministic function of token\\\n634\t    \\ norms），不是 stochastic noise。\\nL2norm 和 random 在 cliff zone 都 crash on same 4\\\n635\t    \\ tasks (T1=cream_cheese, T4=ketchup, T6=butter, T8=chocolate_pudding) → cliff\\\n636\t    \\ 是 architectural， 不是 method-specific。\\n\"\n637\t  tables:\n638\t  - caption: X-VLA Object Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic (L2norm)\n639\t    columns:\n640\t    - k\n641\t    - Tokens Kept\n642\t    - Seed 42\n643\t    - Seed 43\n644\t    - Seed 44\n645\t    - Mean\n646\t    - SD\n647\t    rows:\n648\t    - - '0.90'\n649\t      - '45'\n650\t      - 97.6%\n651\t      - —\n652\t      - 98.2%\n653\t      - 97.6%\n654\t      - —\n655\t    - - '0.85'\n656\t      - '42'\n657\t      - 68.0%\n658\t      - 67.6%\n659\t      - 68.2%\n660\t      - 67.9%\n661\t      - '0.31'\n662\t    - - '0.80'\n663\t      - '40'\n664\t      - 88.8%\n665\t      - 88.4%\n666\t      - 89.8%\n667\t      - 89.0%\n668\t      - '0.72'\n669\t    - - '0.70'\n670\t      - '35'\n671\t      - 56.2%\n672\t      - 59.0%\n673\t      - 56.4%\n674\t      - 57.2%\n675\t      - '1.56'\n676\t  figures_description:\n677\t  - 'Fig: X-VLA Object cliff profile with 3-seed error bars — sharp V-shape at k=0.85,\n678\t    recovery at k=0.80. Annotate ''2 tokens, 21pp gap''.'\n679\t  analysis: 'Cliff localization 完成。Paper 中用 1 figure 展示 X-VLA 的 full pruning curve\n680\t    (k=0.1 to k=0.95)，annotate k=0.85 cliff 和 non-monotonic recovery。 Discussion 中说明\n681\t    BART encoder 的 length-dependent interaction 机制。\n682\t\n683\t    '\n684\t- name: RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler Fine-tune + Pruning\n685\t  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n686\t  description: 'Perceiver Resampler connector 作为第 3 个 connector family 验证。 Training\n687\t    killed twice。Median tier 预测即使完成也不会改变核心结论。\n688\t\n689\t    '\n690\t  expected_results:\n691\t    training_status: killed\n692\t    training_attempts: 2\n693\t    roboflamingo_predicted_cv: 0.18\n694\t    roboflamingo_predicted_entropy: 0.72\n695\t    roboflamingo_predicted_baseline_sr: 55\n696\t    roboflamingo_predicted_k09_sr: 48\n697\t    roboflamingo_predicted_k05_sr: 28\n698\t    would_strengthen_paper: false\n699\t    paper_coverage_without: 5 models × 3 families sufficient for CoRL\n700\t  result_rationale: 'RoboFlamingo training 两次 killed，likely due to (1) Perceiver Resampler\n701\t    与 LIBERO task distribution 的 incompatibility，(2) fine-tuning instability from\n702\t    frozen cross-attention + trainable resampler 的 gradient mismatch。\n703\t\n704\t    即使完成，Perceiver Resampler 的预测 CV=0.18 会落在 X-VLA 和 OpenVLA 之间—— 介于 token-entangling\n705\t    和 token-independent 之间。这不会改变 2-axis framework 的核心结论，只是增加一个中间数据点。\n706\t\n707\t    Median tier 下 5 models × 3 families (linear / MLP / pixel-shuffle) 已经足够 支撑 CoRL\n708\t    submission。Perceiver Resampler 作为 ''future work'' 提及。\n709\t\n710\t    '\n711\t  tables: []\n712\t  figures_description: []\n713\t  analysis: 'Dropped from paper scope。在 Discussion 中提到 ''additional connector families\n714\t    (e.g., Perceiver Resampler, cross-attention based) remain to be validated'' 作为\n715\t    limitation 和 future direction。\n716\t\n717\t    '\n718\t- name: E5 Attention-Based Pruning — X-VLA vs π0.5 Cross-Suite\n719\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n720\t  description: 'Attention-based pruning (E5) 在 X-VLA 和 π0.5 上的 cross-suite 结果。 X-VLA\n721\t    attention pruning 表现极好（Object 99.2%, Long 90.2%）， π0.5 attention 在 Object k=0.7\n722\t    catastrophic (0.6%) 但 Goal 70.2%。 Median tier：Goal 初始 0% 后修复为 98.2%，需额外 seed 确认可靠性。\n723\t\n724\t    '\n725\t  expected_results:\n726\t    xvla_attn_last_k05_object: 99.2\n727\t    xvla_attn_mean_k05_object: 98.4\n728\t    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_object: 97.4\n729\t    xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial: 88.8\n730\t    xvla_attn_mean_k05_spatial: 91.6\n731\t    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_spatial: 92.8\n732\t    xvla_attn_last_k05_goal: 98.2\n733\t    xvla_attn_mean_k05_goal: 97.4\n734\t    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_goal: 96.8\n735\t    xvla_attn_last_k05_long: 90.2\n736\t    xvla_attn_mean_k05_long: 94.0\n737\t    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_long: 94.8\n738\t    xvla_attn_last_k03_object: 84.2\n739\t    xvla_attn_mean_k03_object: 96.0\n740\t    xvla_attn_mean_k03_spatial: 90.4\n741\t    xvla_attn_last_k03_spatial: 85.6\n742\t    pi05_attn_k095_object: 98.4\n743\t    pi05_attn_k09_object: 97.2\n744\t    pi05_attn_k085_object: 92.2\n745\t    pi05_attn_k07_object: 0.6\n746\t    pi05_attn_k05_object: 37.8\n747\t    pi05_attn_k05_spatial: 72.6\n748\t    pi05_attn_k05_goal: 71.2\n749\t    pi05_attn_k05_long: 49.4\n750\t    openvla_attn_k09_object: 61.4\n751\t    openvla_attn_k085_object: 55.0\n752\t    openvla_attn_k09_goal: 73.2\n753\t    openvla_attn_k09_spatial: 80.4\n754\t    xvla_attn_goal_fix_needed: true\n755\t    xvla_attn_goal_seed42_sr: 98.2\n756\t    xvla_attn_goal_seed43_needed: true\n757\t    xvla_attn_goal_predicted_seed43_sr: 97.5\n758\t  result_rationale: 'E5 attention pruning 在不同 model 上表现 divergent：\n759\t\n760\t    X-VLA (BART encoder)：attention pruning 近乎 lossless，因为 BART 的 12-layer self-attention\n761\t    产生了 meaningful attention patterns——high-attention tokens 确实 是最重要的。k=0.5 Object\n762\t    99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → attention 比 L2norm 好 56.6pp。 这是因为 BART encoder 的 attention\n763\t    直接反映了 token 间的 functional dependency。\n764\t\n765\t    Goal suite 初始为 0%（bug），修复后 98.2% → 需要 seed43 确认 fix 是 genuine。 Median tier 预测\n766\t    seed43 = 97.5%（fix 是 valid 的，但需要额外 seed 才能在 paper 中 claim）。\n767\t\n768\t    π0.5 (linear projection)：attention pruning 在 k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%)， 因为 PaliGemma\n769\t    的 per-layer attention 在中间 k 值产生了 adversarial selection。 π0.5 的 attention entropy\n770\t    = 0.666，说明 attention 分布有 moderate sharpness， 但不 correlate with true token importance（CV=0.055\n771\t    说明所有 tokens equally important）。Attention-based pruning 在 uniform-importance model\n772\t    上不可靠。\n773\t\n774\t    OpenVLA (MLP)：attention pruning k=0.9 Object = 61.4% < L2norm = 70.6% < random\n775\t    = 69.2%。 Attention 是三种方法中最差的，因为 MLP connector 后的 attention 也不 reliable predict\n776\t    token importance。\n777\t\n778\t    Paper value：attention pruning 的 effectiveness 也是 connector-dependent， strengthening\n779\t    ''connector determines optimal compression strategy'' claim。\n780\t\n781\t    '\n782\t  tables:\n783\t  - caption: E5 Attention Pruning k=0.5 — Cross-Model Cross-Suite\n784\t    columns:\n785\t    - Model\n786\t    - Object\n787\t    - Spatial\n788\t    - Goal\n789\t    - Long\n790\t    rows:\n791\t    - - X-VLA (attn-last)\n792\t      - 99.2%\n793\t      - 88.8%\n794\t      - 98.2%*\n795\t      - 90.2%\n796\t    - - X-VLA (attn-mean)\n797\t      - 98.4%\n798\t      - 91.6%\n799\t      - 97.4%\n800\t      - 94.0%\n801\t    - - pi0.5 (attn)\n802\t      - 37.8%\n803\t      - 72.6%\n804\t      - 71.2%\n805\t      - 49.4%\n806\t    - - X-VLA (L2norm)\n807\t      - 42.6%\n808\t      - 58.8%\n809\t      - 59.0%\n810\t      - 44.6%\n811\t    - - X-VLA (random)\n812\t      - 70.6%\n813\t      - 71.4%\n814\t      - 67.9%\n815\t      - 61.6%\n816\t  figures_description:\n817\t  - 'Fig: Method comparison radar chart — X-VLA at k=0.5: attention (near-lossless)\n818\t    vs L2norm (42.6%) vs random (70.6%) across 4 suites. Shows attention dominance\n819\t    for BART connector.'\n820\t  analysis: 'E5 attention pruning 提供了 Claim 5 的重要扩展：不只是 L2norm vs random 的 strategy\n821\t    depends on CV，attention-based methods 也是 connector-dependent。 BART connector 的\n822\t    attention 是 reliable signal（因为 12-layer self-attention creates meaningful importance\n823\t    distribution），而 linear/MLP connector 的 attention 不可靠。Paper 中可以加一行 Table showing\n824\t    method effectiveness rank per model。 但 Goal 0%→98.2% 的 fix 需要 seed43 确认，Median\n825\t    tier 下这个 reliability concern 需要在 paper 中 transparent disclosure。\n826\t\n827\t    '\n828\t- name: CV Scaling Law — Spearman Correlation Across Conditions\n829\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n830\t  description: 'CV 作为 pruning strategy predictor 的 Spearman correlation 分析。 Median\n831\t    tier 预测 abs(Spearman) 在 0.6-0.85 之间。\n832\t\n833\t    '\n834\t  expected_results:\n835\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spearman: 0.82\n836\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_p_value: 0.03\n837\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_spearman: 0.75\n838\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_p_value: 0.05\n839\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spearman: 0.45\n840\t    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_p_value: 0.15\n841\t    cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.74\n842\t    n_models_k05: 3\n843\t    n_suites_k05: 1\n844\t    datapoints_k05:\n845\t    - model: pi0.5\n846\t      cv: 0.055\n847\t      gap_pp: -35.4\n848\t    - model: X-VLA\n849\t      cv: 0.151\n850\t      gap_pp: -26.9\n851\t    - model: OpenVLA\n852\t      cv: 0.215\n853\t      gap_pp: 1.8\n854\t    k05_gap_monotonic: true\n855\t    k07_gap_monotonic: true\n856\t    k03_gap_monotonic: false\n857\t  result_rationale: 'CV scaling law 的 Spearman correlation 0.74 落在 median tier range\n858\t    [0.6, 0.85] 中。\n859\t\n860\t    k=0.5 是最 clean 的 scaling law validation point：3 个 model 的 L2norm-random gap 与\n861\t    CV 呈单调关系（-35.4pp → -26.9pp → +1.8pp as CV increases 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215）。 Spearman\n862\t    = 0.82，因为只有 3 个 data points 所以 p-value 边缘显著。\n863\t\n864\t    k=0.7 作为 confirmatory second row：pattern 一致但 gap magnitudes 小（-22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4），\n865\t    Spearman = 0.75。\n866\t\n867\t    k=0.3 BREAKS the scaling law：π0.5 reversal (+18.9pp L2norm wins) 但 X-VLA random\n868\t    仍大幅领先 (+42.3pp)。这不是 CV 不好，而是 absolute token budget 的交互效应： π0.5 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（大\n869\t    budget），X-VLA k=0.3 保留 15 tokens（小 budget）。 Large budget + low CV = L2norm 可以\n870\t    fragment clusters 恢复 diversity。 Small budget + mid CV = 无论如何都太少，random 保持 stochastic\n871\t    diversity 的优势。\n872\t\n873\t    Paper strategy：k=0.5 作为 main table，k=0.7 作为 confirmatory。k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion\n874\t    中说明，强调 ''CV predicts strategy preference at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7);\n875\t    at extreme compression (k=0.3), absolute token budget introduces additional interaction''。Claim\n876\t    5 加限定 ''at moderate compression''。\n877\t\n878\t    '\n879\t  tables:\n880\t  - caption: CV Scaling Law — L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) at k=0.5 and k=0.7\n881\t    columns:\n882\t    - Model\n883\t    - CV\n884\t    - Gap k=0.7 (pp)\n885\t    - Gap k=0.5 (pp)\n886\t    - Gap k=0.3 (pp)\n887\t    rows:\n888\t    - - pi0.5\n889\t      - '0.055'\n890\t      - '-22.2'\n891\t      - '-35.4'\n892\t      - '+18.9'\n893\t    - - X-VLA\n894\t      - '0.151'\n895\t      - '-6.5'\n896\t      - '-26.9'\n897\t      - '-42.3'\n898\t    - - OpenVLA\n899\t      - '0.215'\n900\t      - '+5.4'\n901\t      - '+1.8'\n902\t      - '+3.6'\n903\t  - caption: 'Spearman Correlation: CV vs Strategy Gap'\n904\t    columns:\n905\t    - k value\n906\t    - Spearman rho\n907\t    - p-value\n908\t    - Monotonic?\n909\t    rows:\n910\t    - - '0.7'\n911\t      - '0.75'\n912\t      - '0.05'\n913\t      - 'Yes'\n914\t    - - '0.5'\n915\t      - '0.82'\n916\t      - '0.03'\n917\t      - 'Yes'\n918\t    - - '0.3'\n919\t      - '0.45'\n920\t      - '0.15'\n921\t      - No (reversal)\n922\t  figures_description:\n923\t  - 'Fig: Scatter plot with regression line — CV (x-axis) vs L2norm-Random gap (y-axis)\n924\t    at k=0.5. Three points with clear positive trend. Annotate Spearman=0.82.'\n925\t  analysis: 'Claim 5 survives review but需要加限定。原 claim ''CV predicts optimal pruning\n926\t    strategy'' 改为 ''CV predicts optimal pruning strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)''。\n927\t    k=0.3 reversal 说明 strategy preference = f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget)， 不是仅 CV\n928\t    决定。这个 nuance 在 median tier 下是可以接受的——reviewers 会 appreciate honest boundary conditions。3-4\n929\t    个 claims survive review 的预测中，这个 claim 以 qualified form survive。\n930\t\n931\t    '\n932\t- name: SmolVLA VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Consolidation + Architecture Control\n933\t  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n934\t  description: 'VTR M-sweep (M=16/32/64/96/128) 的 3-seed 最终结果 + MLP adapter 对照。 已有大量数据，Median\n935\t    tier 下 consolidate 最终 statistics。\n936\t\n937\t    '\n938\t  expected_results:\n939\t    vtr_m16_3seed_mean: 56.9\n940\t    vtr_m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n941\t    vtr_m16_3seed_seeds:\n942\t    - 55.8\n943\t    - 58.4\n944\t    - 56.5\n945\t    vtr_m32_3seed_mean: 60.1\n946\t    vtr_m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n947\t    vtr_m32_3seed_seeds:\n948\t    - 61.6\n949\t    - 59.2\n950\t    - 59.6\n951\t    vtr_m64_3seed_mean: 62.0\n952\t    vtr_m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n953\t    vtr_m64_3seed_seeds:\n954\t    - 61.6\n955\t    - 60.0\n956\t    - 64.4\n957\t    vtr_m96_3seed_mean: 54.5\n958\t    vtr_m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n959\t    vtr_m96_3seed_seeds:\n960\t    - 52.6\n961\t    - 58.2\n962\t    - 52.8\n963\t    vtr_m128_3seed_mean: 58.0\n964\t    vtr_m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n965\t    vtr_m128_3seed_seeds:\n966\t    - 59.8\n967\t    - 54.0\n968\t    - 60.2\n969\t    m_curve_range_pp: 7.5\n970\t    m_curve_vs_baseline_max_diff: 5.3\n971\t    m_curve_flat: true\n972\t    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean: 63.4\n973\t    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std: 2.6\n974\t    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_seeds:\n975\t    - 65.2\n976\t    - 64.6\n977\t    - 60.4\n978\t    vtc_vs_mlp_t_stat: 1.94\n979\t    vtc_vs_mlp_p_value: 0.15\n980\t    architecture_independent: true\n981\t    smolvla_baseline: 59.2\n982\t    hard_prune_k05: 0\n983\t    recovery_from_zero: true\n984\t  result_rationale: 'VTR M-sweep 确认 M-curve 是 flat 的：M=16 (56.9%) 到 M=128 (58.0%)，\n985\t    all within ±5pp of baseline 59.2%。这意味着 VTR 对 pixel-shuffle connector 实现了 near-lossless\n986\t    compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%)。\n987\t\n988\t    M=64 是 absolute best (62.0%)，M=96 是 lowest (54.5%) 但 p=0.034 与 M=64 的差异 statistically\n989\t    significant——M=96 的 higher variance (3.2pp) 和 lower mean 可能是因为 96-token representation\n990\t    落在 an awkward regime：不够多以 passthrough (M=128)，但 compression ratio 不够大 to force\n991\t    useful abstraction (M=32/64)。\n992\t\n993\t    MLP adapter (63.4%) vs VTC (60.1%) p=0.15 → architecture independent。 任何 learned\n994\t    re-encoding 都能从 0% 恢复到 baseline。\n995\t\n996\t    Median tier 下 VTR 的 contribution statement 明确：''VTR achieves near-lossless compression\n997\t    at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors, recovering from 0% (hard pruning) to\n998\t    ~59% (baseline)''。不 overclaim 超过 baseline。\n999\t\n1000\t    '\n1001\t  tables:\n1002\t  - caption: VTR M-Sweep — 3-Seed Statistics (SmolVLA Object)\n1003\t    columns:\n1004\t    - M\n1005\t    - Compression\n1006\t    - Mean SR (%)\n1007\t    - Std (pp)\n1008\t    - vs Baseline\n1009\t    rows:\n1010\t    - - '16'\n1011\t      - 87.5%\n1012\t      - '56.9'\n1013\t      - '1.3'\n1014\t      - -2.3pp\n1015\t    - - '32'\n1016\t      - 75.0%\n1017\t      - '60.1'\n1018\t      - '1.3'\n1019\t      - +0.9pp\n1020\t    - - '64'\n1021\t      - 50.0%\n1022\t      - '62.0'\n1023\t      - '2.3'\n1024\t      - +2.8pp\n1025\t    - - '96'\n1026\t      - 25.0%\n1027\t      - '54.5'\n1028\t      - '3.2'\n1029\t      - -4.7pp\n1030\t    - - '128'\n1031\t      - 0% (pass)\n1032\t      - '58.0'\n1033\t      - '3.5'\n1034\t      - -1.2pp\n1035\t    - - MLP-32\n1036\t      - 75.0%\n1037\t      - '63.4'\n1038\t      - '2.6'\n1039\t      - +4.2pp\n1040\t  figures_description:\n1041\t  - 'Fig: M-curve with error bars — flat profile, all within baseline ±5pp band (shaded).\n1042\t    Hard prune reference at 0%.'\n1043\t  analysis: 'VTR results 完备。Paper 中用 M-curve figure + architecture control table 支撑\n1044\t    Claim 4。Key limitation：仅对 pixel-shuffle 有效（OpenVLA 0%）， method contribution 限于\n1045\t    worst-case architecture。\n1046\t\n1047\t    '\n1048\t- name: Claims Survival Under Review — Median Tier Assessment\n1049\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n1050\t  description: '5 个 core claims 在 median tier 下的 review survival 预测。 预测 3-4 个 claims\n1051\t    survive。\n1052\t\n1053\t    '\n1054\t  expected_results:\n1055\t    claims_surviving: 3.5\n1056\t    claim_1_2axis_framework:\n1057\t      status: survives with qualification\n1058\t      original: governed by two axes\n1059\t      revised: primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity\n1060\t        as a modulating factor for token-entangling connectors\n1061\t      qualification: Axis-2 amplification weak for token-independent connectors (π0.5)\n1062\t      strength: 0.8\n1063\t    claim_2_pixel_shuffle_entanglement:\n1064\t      status: survives fully\n1065\t      evidence: 7 conditions × 4 suites × official checkpoint → 0%\n1066\t      strength: 1.0\n1067\t    claim_3_graded_degradation:\n1068\t      status: survives fully\n1069\t      evidence: OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT CV/entropy confirmation\n1070\t      strength: 0.95\n1071\t    claim_4_vtr_recovery:\n1072\t      status: survives with limitation\n1073\t      original: universal compression via VTR\n1074\t      revised: VTR recovers pixel-shuffle from 0% to baseline; ineffective for MLP\n1075\t        projector\n1076\t      limitation: method contribution narrowed to pixel-shuffle-specific\n1077\t      strength: 0.7\n1078\t    claim_5_cv_scaling_law:\n1079\t      status: survives with boundary condition\n1080\t      original: CV predicts optimal strategy\n1081\t      revised: CV predicts optimal strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)\n1082\t      boundary: k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models with large token budgets\n1083\t      strength: 0.75\n1084\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 预测 3.5 claims survive（3 full + 1.5 qualified），落在\n1085\t    [3, 4] range。\n1086\t\n1087\t    Claim 2（pixel-shuffle entanglement）是最 robust 的——0% at k=0.95, all methods, all\n1088\t    suites, official checkpoint, dual-seed confirmed。没有任何 edge case。\n1089\t\n1090\t    Claim 3（graded degradation）也 robust——OpenVLA 6-point curve 是 clean monotonic，\n1091\t    OFT CV/entropy confirmation 是 clean controlled comparison。\n1092\t\n1093\t    Claim 1（2-axis framework）需要 qualification 因为 Axis-2 对 token-independent connectors\n1094\t    的 amplification 弱于预期。Paper 不能说 ''task complexity always amplifies pruning sensitivity''，而是\n1095\t    ''task complexity amplifies sensitivity SPECIFICALLY for token-entangling connectors\n1096\t    where pruning damage cascades''。\n1097\t\n1098\t    Claim 4（VTR）的 method contribution 收窄——OpenVLA 0% 意味着 VTR 不是 universal。 Reviewers\n1099\t    可能 question: ''if VTR only works on pixel-shuffle, and pixel-shuffle is the architecture\n1100\t    you''re warning against, isn''t the method contribution circular?'' Response:\n1101\t    ''VTR provides a migration path for existing pixel-shuffle VLAs, not a design\n1102\t    recommendation for new ones.''\n1103\t\n1104\t    Claim 5（CV scaling law）加 boundary condition 后仍有价值——k=0.5-0.7 的 scaling law 是 clean\n1105\t    的（Spearman 0.75-0.82），只是 k=0.3 有 reversal。\n1106\t\n1107\t    '\n1108\t  tables:\n1109\t  - caption: Claims Survival Assessment — Median Tier\n1110\t    columns:\n1111\t    - Claim\n1112\t    - Original Strength\n1113\t    - Median Tier Status\n1114\t    - Revised Strength\n1115\t    rows:\n1116\t    - - 'C1: 2-Axis Framework'\n1117\t      - Strong\n1118\t      - Qualified\n1119\t      - '0.80'\n1120\t    - - 'C2: Pixel-Shuffle'\n1121\t      - Strong\n1122\t      - Fully Survives\n1123\t      - '1.00'\n1124\t    - - 'C3: Graded Degradation'\n1125\t      - Strong\n1126\t      - Fully Survives\n1127\t      - '0.95'\n1128\t    - - 'C4: VTR Recovery'\n1129\t      - Moderate\n1130\t      - Limited to pixel-shuffle\n1131\t      - '0.70'\n1132\t    - - 'C5: CV Scaling Law'\n1133\t      - Moderate\n1134\t      - Boundary at k=0.3\n1135\t      - '0.75'\n1136\t  figures_description: []\n1137\t  analysis: Paper identity 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method'。 Title 改为\n1138\t    'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'—— 更保守但准确。Contribution\n1139\t    statement 聚焦：(1) first systematic cross-architecture token pruning analysis in\n1140\t    VLAs (5 models × 4 suites), (2) CV as zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance\n1141\t    AND strategy, (3) VTR as targeted recovery method for worst-case (pixel-shuffle)\n1142\t    connectors。仍提交 CoRL。\n1143\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f75ff7-cbcf-4297-8f4a-a59d253e665c","uuid":"a97ee9a5-3099-4f14-81be-e8334cb9e74b","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:09:17.374Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T050917/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '2-axis framework directionally correct but需要 qualify 2-3 个 edge\n  cases。 Claim 1 弱化为 ''primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity\n  as a modulating factor''。 Claim 5 加限定 ''at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)''，k=0.3\n  reversal 移入 Discussion。 VTR 明确为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。Paper identity 从\n  ''analysis + method'' 调整为 ''primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case\n  architecture''。 Title 改为更保守的 ''How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness\n  in VLAs''。 仍提交 CoRL，contribution statement 聚焦 diagnostic insight。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: π0.5 4-Suite Pruning Characterization — Median Tier Consolidation\n  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n  description: 'π0.5 (4B, PaliGemma linear proj, CV=0.055) 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 的 pruning\n    response。 Median tier 预测：Object 上 random cliff (k=0.85-0.925) 是 Object-specific\n    而非 universal； Goal/Long 上 Axis-2 amplification 弱于 X-VLA (<15pp for π0.5 vs 27.8pp\n    for X-VLA)。 CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pi05_baseline_object: 98.2\n    pi05_baseline_spatial: 97.2\n    pi05_baseline_goal: 96.4\n    pi05_baseline_long: 92.8\n    pi05_cv: 0.055\n    pi05_random_k095_object_sr: 72.5\n    pi05_random_k0925_object_sr: 28.8\n    pi05_random_k09_object_sr: 10.2\n    pi05_random_k085_object_sr: 4.4\n    pi05_random_k07_object_sr: 75.5\n    pi05_random_k05_object_sr: 68.9\n    pi05_random_k03_object_sr: 34.3\n    pi05_l2norm_k095_object_sr: 98.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k0925_object_sr: 99.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr: 98.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr: 98.0\n    pi05_l2norm_k07_object_sr: 56.4\n    pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr: 33.5\n    pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr: 53.2\n    pi05_random_k095_spatial_sr: 76.6\n    pi05_random_k0925_spatial_sr: 59.3\n    pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr: 54.0\n    pi05_random_k085_spatial_sr: 58.8\n    pi05_random_k07_spatial_sr: 74.1\n    pi05_random_k05_spatial_sr: 72.0\n    pi05_random_k03_spatial_sr: 48.4\n    pi05_l2norm_k095_spatial_sr: 97.9\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr: 95.3\n    pi05_l2norm_k085_spatial_sr: 88.8\n    pi05_l2norm_k07_spatial_sr: 67.7\n    pi05_l2norm_k05_spatial_sr: 55.7\n    pi05_l2norm_k03_spatial_sr: 55.0\n    pi05_random_k095_goal_sr: 83.5\n    pi05_random_k09_goal_sr: 61.7\n    pi05_random_k085_goal_sr: 52.6\n    pi05_random_k07_goal_sr: 76.9\n    pi05_random_k05_goal_sr: 73.6\n    pi05_random_k03_goal_sr: 51.7\n    pi05_l2norm_k095_goal_sr: 90.1\n    pi05_l2norm_k0925_goal_sr: 89.6\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr: 89.8\n    pi05_l2norm_k085_goal_sr: 87.5\n    pi05_l2norm_k07_goal_sr: 72.0\n    pi05_l2norm_k05_goal_sr: 59.5\n    pi05_l2norm_k03_goal_sr: 51.8\n    pi05_random_k095_long_sr: 62.2\n    pi05_random_k09_long_sr: 31.3\n    pi05_random_k085_long_sr: 44.3\n    pi05_random_k07_long_sr: 66.3\n    pi05_random_k05_long_sr: 47.6\n    pi05_random_k03_long_sr: 28.7\n    pi05_l2norm_k095_long_sr: 87.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr: 80.3\n    pi05_l2norm_k085_long_sr: 78.8\n    pi05_l2norm_k07_long_sr: 63.5\n    pi05_l2norm_k05_long_sr: 51.4\n    pi05_l2norm_k03_long_sr: 37.5\n    axis2_amplification_object_pp: 88.0\n    axis2_amplification_spatial_pp: 43.2\n    axis2_amplification_goal_pp: 34.7\n    axis2_amplification_long_pp: 61.5\n    pi05_axis2_object_vs_goal_random_k09_pp: -51.5\n    pi05_axis2_object_vs_spatial_random_k09_pp: -43.8\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_object_pp: -35.4\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spatial_pp: -16.3\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_goal_pp: -14.1\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_long_pp: 3.8\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_object_pp: 18.9\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spatial_pp: 6.6\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_goal_pp: 0.1\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_long_pp: 8.8\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 下 π0.5 数据呈现三个关键 pattern：\n\n    (1) Random cliff 是 Object-specific。Object suite 在 k=0.85-0.925 出现灾难性 dip (5%→10.8%→27.6%)，但\n    Spatial 的 floor 保持在 54% 以上，Goal 在 k=0.9 仍有 61.7%。 这是因为 Object 任务需要精确的 object identity\n    discrimination（视觉相似物体间区分）， 而 random 在 cliff zone 恰好破坏了 concentrated critical tokens。Spatial\n    的关键信息 是分布式的（layout patches），Goal 的关键信息由 language 部分承载。\n\n    (2) Axis-2 amplification 对 π0.5 表现为 REVERSED pattern：Goal 和 Spatial 在 k=0.9 random\n    下反而 BETTER than Object（61.7% vs 10.2%）。这与 X-VLA 的 pattern 完全相反 （X-VLA Goal k=0.9\n    比 Object 差 27.8pp）。原因：token-independent connector 下， pruning damage 是 local 的，不会\n    cascade。Object 的 cliff 是 random sampling 的 统计效应（concentrated critical tokens），不是\n    task complexity amplification。 因此 median tier 预测 π0.5 的 Axis-2 amplification <15pp（如果排除\n    Object cliff zone）， 需要在 paper 中 qualify 2-axis framework 对 token-independent connector\n    的适用性。\n\n    (3) CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立：L2norm-random gap = -35.4pp（Object），与 CV=0.055 的极低值一致。但\n    k=0.3 出现 reversal：L2norm 反而 +18.9pp 领先。这是因为 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（足够大的 budget），L2norm\n    的 spatial clustering 在此 budget 下 反而 fragment 成多个 cluster，恢复了 spatial coverage。k=0.5\n    是 clustering 最严重的 sweet spot（1 cluster, 100% concentration, 78% coverage）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random Pruning — Cliff Zone Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - k=0.95\n    - k=0.925\n    - k=0.9\n    - k=0.85\n    - k=0.7\n    - k=0.5\n    - k=0.3\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - 72.5%\n      - 28.8%\n      - 10.2%\n      - 4.4%\n      - 75.5%\n      - 68.9%\n      - 34.3%\n    - - Spatial\n      - 76.6%\n      - 59.3%\n      - 54.0%\n      - 58.8%\n      - 74.1%\n      - 72.0%\n      - 48.4%\n    - - Goal\n      - 83.5%\n      - —\n      - 61.7%\n      - 52.6%\n      - 76.9%\n      - 73.6%\n      - 51.7%\n    - - Long\n      - 62.2%\n      - —\n      - 31.3%\n      - 44.3%\n      - 66.3%\n      - 47.6%\n      - 28.7%\n  - caption: π0.5 L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) — CV Scaling Law Validation\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - k=0.7\n    - k=0.5\n    - k=0.3\n    - Pattern\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - '-19.1'\n      - '-35.4'\n      - '+18.9'\n      - Reversal at k=0.3\n    - - Spatial\n      - '-6.4'\n      - '-16.3'\n      - '+6.6'\n      - Reversal at k=0.3\n    - - Goal\n      - '-4.9'\n      - '-14.1'\n      - '+0.1'\n      - Near-zero at k=0.3\n    - - Long\n      - '-2.8'\n      - '+3.8'\n      - '+8.8'\n      - L2norm consistently better\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: π0.5 random pruning cliff profile — Object (deep V-shape dip to 4.4% at\n    k=0.85) vs Spatial (gradual, floor >54%) vs Goal/Long. Key visual: Object-specific\n    catastrophic collapse.'\n  - 'Fig: L2norm-Random gap vs keep ratio across 4 suites — showing k=0.5 as peak\n    random advantage and k=0.3 reversal point.'\n  analysis: 'Median tier 下需要在 paper 中加 qualification：2-axis framework 的 Axis-2 (task\n    complexity) 对 token-independent connector 的 amplification effect 显著弱于 token-entangling\n    connector。 π0.5 的 suite-dependent sensitivity 主要由 Object cliff（random sampling\n    + concentrated critical tokens 的统计效应）驱动，而非 task complexity amplification。 Claim\n    1 需弱化为 ''connector architecture is the primary determinant; task complexity is\n    a modulating factor primarily for token-entangling connectors''。 CV scaling law\n    (Claim 5) 在 k=0.5 清晰成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论—— Long suite 在所有 k 值 L2norm 都不差于\n    random，可能是 Long 任务的 multi-step 结构 使得 importance-based selection 的 token 恰好 cover\n    关键 subgoal transitions。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Suite Framework Validation — 5 Models × 4 Suites\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: '将 pruning 实验从 LIBERO-Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。 验证 2-axis framework\n    跨 suite 的预测准确性。 Median tier 预测 framework accuracy 75-90%。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    xvla_baseline_object: 99.2\n    xvla_baseline_spatial: 93.0\n    xvla_baseline_goal: 98.4\n    xvla_baseline_long: 94.0\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_object: 97.6\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial: 78.8\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_goal: 70.2\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_long: 27.5\n    xvla_random_k09_object: 97.8\n    xvla_random_k09_spatial: 77.8\n    xvla_random_k09_goal: 70.6\n    xvla_random_k09_long: 29.6\n    xvla_drop_k09_object_pp: 1.6\n    xvla_drop_k09_spatial_pp: 14.2\n    xvla_drop_k09_goal_pp: 28.2\n    xvla_drop_k09_long_pp: 66.5\n    xvla_l2norm_k05_object: 43.4\n    xvla_random_k05_object: 70.3\n    xvla_l2norm_k05_spatial: 58.9\n    xvla_random_k05_spatial: 71.4\n    xvla_l2norm_k05_goal: 59.5\n    xvla_random_k05_goal: 67.9\n    xvla_l2norm_k05_long: 44.8\n    xvla_random_k05_long: 61.6\n    smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n    smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n    smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n    smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n    smolvla_k095_all_suites_all_methods: 0\n    framework_correct_predictions: 17\n    framework_total_predictions: 20\n    framework_accuracy_pct: 85\n    edge_case_1: π0.5 Axis-2 reversed — Goal BETTER than Object at k=0.9\n    edge_case_2: X-VLA Long k=0.85 non-monotonic (35%) < k=0.5 (61.6%)\n    edge_case_3: CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier framework accuracy ~85%：20 个 cross-suite predictions\n    中 17 个正确。\n\n    正确的 predictions： - X-VLA Axis-2 amplification Object→Goal/Long（confirmed 27.8pp/66.5pp）\n    - SmolVLA all suites cliff-edge（confirmed 0% everywhere） - OpenVLA graded degradation\n    across suites - CV scaling law at k=0.5（L2norm-random gap correlates with CV）\n    - L2norm plateau for π0.5 at k≥0.85 on all suites\n\n    需要 qualify 的 edge cases： (1) π0.5 的 Axis-2 pattern 是 reversed（Object WORST, not\n    Goal/Long），因为 token-independent connector 下 task complexity 不 amplify damage，而\n    Object 的 concentrated critical tokens 在 random cliff zone 反而最脆弱。 (2) X-VLA Long\n    k=0.85 出现 non-monotonic reversal（35% < k=0.5 的 61.6%）， 与 Object 的 non-monotonic\n    pattern 不同——Long 的 cliff zone 在更高 k 值， 因为 multi-step reasoning 对 token density\n    的 threshold 更高。 (3) CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal 限制了 Claim 5 的适用范围。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 2-Axis Framework — X-VLA Pruning Drop at k=0.9 Across Suites\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline\n    - L2norm k=0.9\n    - Drop (pp)\n    - Axis-2 Level\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - 99.2%\n      - 97.6%\n      - '-1.6'\n      - Simple\n    - - Spatial\n      - 93.0%\n      - 78.8%\n      - '-14.2'\n      - Moderate\n    - - Goal\n      - 98.4%\n      - 70.2%\n      - '-28.2'\n      - Complex\n    - - Long\n      - 94.0%\n      - 27.5%\n      - '-66.5'\n      - Most Complex\n  - caption: Cross-Suite L2norm vs Random Gap at k=0.5 (pp) — CV Scaling Law\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    rows:\n    - - pi0.5\n      - '0.055'\n      - '-35.4'\n      - '-16.3'\n      - '-14.1'\n      - '+3.8'\n    - - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - '-26.9'\n      - '-12.5'\n      - '-8.4'\n      - '-16.8'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - '+1.8'\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Heatmap of pruning drop (pp from baseline) — 5 models × 4 suites × k=0.9.\n    Visual shows clear Axis-1 (rows) and Axis-2 (columns) gradients for X-VLA/SmolVLA,\n    but flat for π0.5/OpenVLA across suites.'\n  analysis: 'Framework accuracy 85% 落在 median tier range [75%, 90%] 中。3 个 edge cases\n    需要在 paper 中 qualify：(1) 对 π0.5 等 token-independent model，用 ''connector architecture\n    determines base sensitivity; task semantics modulate through statistical token\n    criticality rather than cascading damage'' 替代原先的 ''task complexity amplifies''。\n    (2) X-VLA Long 的 non-monotonic pattern 需要额外 figure 说明 cliff zone 随 task complexity\n    右移。(3) k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion 中说明 CV scaling law 的边界条件。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR SmolVLA Cross-Suite Recovery (M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n  description: 'VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long 上的 recovery 验证。 已有数据：M=32 Spatial=53.2%,\n    Goal=56.4%。 Median tier 预测 recovery ratio 0.9-1.0。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n    smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n    smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n    smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n    smolvla_prune_k05_all_suites: 0\n    vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1\n    vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2\n    vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4\n    vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.0\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_long: 0.956\n    vtr_mean_recovery_ratio: 0.96\n    vtr_m16_object_sr: 56.9\n    vtr_m32_object_sr_confirmed: 60.1\n    vtr_m64_object_sr: 62.0\n    vtr_m96_object_sr: 54.5\n    vtr_m128_object_sr: 58.0\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 下 VTR 在所有 suites 都能从 0%（hard pruning）恢复到 near-baseline，\n    但 recovery ratio 有 suite-dependent variation（0.928-1.193）。\n\n    Object (recovery 1.015): VTR 在 Object 上 recovery 最稳定，因为 Object 任务的 visual discriminability\n    需求可以被 re-encoded tokens 完整保留——pixel-shuffle 的 spatial entanglement 是 Object failure\n    的唯一原因，VTR 修复了这个 entanglement。\n\n    Spatial (recovery 1.193): 看似超过 baseline 但需注意 baseline 是 official checkpoint (44.6%)\n    vs VTR 是 LoRA-FT + VTC (53.2%)——实际上是不同 training pipeline 的差异， 不应解读为 VTR 超越。Paper\n    中需要用 recovery from 0% 而非 absolute comparison。\n\n    Goal (recovery 0.928): 轻微低于 baseline（-4.4pp），因为 VTR 是在 Object suite 训练的， Goal\n    的 multi-step task structure 引入了 distribution shift。Token re-encoding 恢复了 spatial\n    information 但无法完全补偿 task-distribution mismatch。\n\n    Long (predicted 0.956): Long 的 baseline 最低（36.6%），VTR 的 re-encoding 在 simple manipulation\n    primitives 上有效，但 Long 需要跨多个 sub-goal 的 temporal coherence， VTR 的 per-step re-encoding\n    无法显式捕捉 cross-step dependencies。预测 recovery ~35%， 略低于 baseline 但远高于 0%。\n\n    关键限定：VTR 仅对 pixel-shuffle connector 有效（OpenVLA M=128 = 0%），method contribution\n    限于 ''targeted solution for worst-case architecture''。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery from Cliff-Edge\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline\n    - Hard Prune k=0.5\n    - VTR M=32\n    - Recovery Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - 59.2%\n      - 0%\n      - 60.1%\n      - '1.015'\n    - - Spatial\n      - 44.6%*\n      - 0%\n      - 53.2%\n      - 1.193*\n    - - Goal\n      - 60.8%\n      - 0%\n      - 56.4%\n      - '0.928'\n    - - Long\n      - 36.6%\n      - 0%\n      - ~35.0%\n      - ~0.956\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Bar chart — SmolVLA Baseline vs Hard Prune vs VTR M=32 across 4 suites.\n    Visual emphasis on recovery from 0% (red) to near-baseline (green).'\n  analysis: 'VTR 的 mean recovery ratio 0.96 落在 median tier range [0.9, 1.0] 中。 Method\n    contribution 需明确限定为 pixel-shuffle-specific：(1) 只在 SmolVLA 上有效， (2) 在非 Object suite\n    上有 -4.4pp 到 +8.6pp 的 variance，(3) OpenVLA VTR = 0%。 Paper identity 从 ''analysis\n    + method'' 调整为 ''primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case architecture''。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR/VTC on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — Universality Falsification\n  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n  description: 'VTR M=128 已确认 0% SR（overfitting）。VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress。\n    Median tier 预测 VTC-only 也失败，VTR 限于 pixel-shuffle。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_vtr_m128_20k_sr: 0\n    openvla_baseline_object_sr: 74\n    openvla_vtc_m32_sr: 0\n    openvla_vtc_m64_sr: 0\n    openvla_vtc_m96_sr: 0\n    openvla_vtc_m32_train_loss: 2.5\n    openvla_vtc_m64_train_loss: 2.4\n    openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 预测 VTC-only M=32/M=64 也会失败，原因是 MLP projector tokens\n    已经是 individually meaningful 的——re-encoding 增加了不必要的 bottleneck，导致 overfitting。\n\n    具体机制：OpenVLA 的 3-layer MLP connector 将 SigLIP features 映射为 256 个独立的 vision tokens，每个\n    token 保留了原始 spatial meaning。VTR/VTC 在这些 tokens 上 添加 cross-attention / MLP adapter\n    作为 bottleneck，但这些 tokens 不需要 ''re-encoding''——它们的 spatial information 没有被 entangle。额外的\n    bottleneck 反而限制了 information flow，导致模型 overfit 到 training set 的 action distribution。\n\n    实际 training logs 显示 M=128 在 20K steps 后 output 是 identical action（所有 observation\n    产生相同的 action sequence），这是 severe mode collapse 的 hallmark。 M=32/M=64 的更强 compression\n    会加剧而非缓解这个问题。\n\n    Training 失败的 root cause 也可能是 OpenVLA 的 7B model size 导致 VTC 的 22M params 相对过小（0.3%\n    of model）——gradient signal 在 backprop 过程中被 diluted。\n\n    这个 negative result 反而 strengthens 论文：VTR 的有效性是 connector-dependent 的， 验证了 ''connector\n    determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy''。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: VTR/VTC on OpenVLA vs SmolVLA — Connector-Dependent Effectiveness\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Connector\n    - CV\n    - VTR M=128\n    - VTC M=32\n    - VTC M=64\n    rows:\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - Pixel-shuffle\n      - '0.314'\n      - 58.0%\n      - 60.1%\n      - 62.0%\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - 3-layer MLP\n      - '0.215'\n      - 0%\n      - ~0%*\n      - ~0%*\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Training loss curves — SmolVLA VTC (converges to ~0.05) vs OpenVLA VTC (plateaus\n    at ~2.5, fails to converge). Annotate divergence point.'\n  analysis: 'VTR universality falsified。Method contribution 收窄为 pixel-shuffle-specific\n    solution。 Paper 中将 VTR 定位为 ''targeted re-encoding for architectures where token\n    pruning creates irreversible information loss''。Discussion 中指出 MLP projector VLAs\n    应 直接用 simple pruning（L2norm 或 random depending on CV），不需要 learned compression。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96) — Training Convergence Test\n  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n  description: 'OpenVLA 上 VTC-only training（不冻结 backbone），测试不同 M 值。 Training 已 failed/killed\n    on all M values。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_vtc_m32_status: failed\n    openvla_vtc_m64_status: failed\n    openvla_vtc_m96_status: failed\n    openvla_vtc_m96_final_loss: 2.45\n    openvla_vtc_m64_final_loss: null\n    interpretation: VTC training does not converge on MLP-projector VLAs\n  result_rationale: 'All M values 的 VTC training 在 OpenVLA 上失败或 killed。M=96 跑完了 100K\n    steps 但 final loss 2.45（远高于 SmolVLA 的 ~0.05），说明模型未能学到有效的 token re-encoding。M=64\n    和 M=32 的 VTC-only training 也 crashed/failed。\n\n    Root cause：OpenVLA (7B) 是 frozen backbone + 22M compressor 的极端不平衡。 SmolVLA (450M)\n    的 compressor/backbone ratio = 22M/450M = 4.9%，而 OpenVLA 的 ratio = 22M/7B = 0.3%。VTC\n    的 gradient signal 在通过 7B frozen backbone 的 attention layers 时被严重 attenuate，导致\n    compressor 无法学到有用的 representation。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'OpenVLA VTC M-sweep 的 universal failure 进一步确认 VTR/VTC 仅对 pixel-shuffle\n    connector 有效。Paper 中在 Table 5 或 supplementary 中报告这些 negative results， 强化 ''VTR\n    effectiveness is connector-dependent'' 的 claim。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA-OFT Cross-Suite Pruning (Blocked by GPU Incompatibility)\n  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n  description: 'OFT (7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fused, 512 tokens) 在 4 suites\n    上的 baseline + pruning。Blocked by Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility。 Median tier\n    用 CV/entropy analysis 替代 SR eval。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    oft_cv: 0.219\n    oft_entropy: 0.667\n    oft_tokens: 512\n    oft_baseline_official_sr: 97\n    oft_predicted_k09_sr: 65\n    oft_predicted_k07_sr: 50\n    oft_predicted_k05_sr: 38\n    oft_predicted_k03_sr: 22\n    oft_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp: -2\n    oft_l2norm_advantage_mild_k: true\n    blocker: Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility — requires A100 + torch 2.2\n  result_rationale: 'OFT eval 被 Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA 不兼容 blocked。Median tier 下仅用 diagnostic\n    metrics 参与分析：CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA (0.215)，entropy=0.667 ≈ OpenVLA (0.661)。\n\n    这两个 near-identical diagnostic values 预测 OFT 的 pruning behavior 与 OpenVLA 几乎一致——graded\n    degradation，L2norm 在 aggressive k 略优于 random。 512 tokens (vs OpenVLA 的 256) 意味着\n    absolute token budget 在 same k ratio 下 更大（k=0.5 保留 256 vs 128），可能导致略好的 SR，但 degradation\n    PATTERN 应相同。\n\n    关键 paper value：OFT 用了不同的 action head（Optimal Flow Transport vs standard）， 但 CV\n    和 entropy 几乎 identical → 确认 connector（not action head）determines attention structure\n    和 pruning behavior。这是一个 clean controlled comparison。\n\n    Median tier 下 OFT 作为 supplementary evidence 出现（CV/entropy table）， 不作为 primary\n    experimental evidence。Cite official baseline ~97%， acknowledge eval 未能完成。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Connector vs Action Head — Diagnostic Decoupling\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Action Head\n    - Connector\n    - CV\n    - Entropy\n    rows:\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Standard (MLP)\n      - 3-layer MLP\n      - '0.215'\n      - '0.661'\n    - - OpenVLA-OFT\n      - OFT (flow)\n      - 3-layer MLP\n      - '0.219'\n      - '0.667'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of CV vs Entropy for all 6 models — OFT and OpenVLA as overlapping\n    points, confirming connector-dominance over action-head.'\n  analysis: 'OFT 贡献收窄为 diagnostic decoupling evidence。Paper 中用一句话总结： ''OFT (CV=0.219)\n    ≈ Standard OpenVLA (CV=0.215) despite different action heads, confirming that\n    connector architecture, not downstream components, determines token importance\n    distribution.'' Eval SR 不可得，acknowledged as limitation。\n\n    '\n- name: OFT Token Importance CV Measurement\n  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n  description: 'OFT importance CV 测量，完成 6-model diagnostic table 的最后一个空位。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    oft_importance_cv: 0.219\n    oft_importance_cv_std: 0.012\n    oft_importance_gini: 0.11\n    oft_n_tokens: 512\n    spectrum_position: between OpenVLA (0.215) and SmolVLA (0.314)\n  result_rationale: 'OFT 使用与 OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector（GELU activation），唯一差异是\n    (1) fused DINOv2+SigLIP encoder 产生 512 tokens（vs OpenVLA 的 256）， (2) OFT action\n    head。Entropy 已确认 0.667 ≈ 0.661，CV 预测 0.219 ≈ 0.215。 微小的 CV 差异（+0.004）可能来自 DINOv2\n    features 的 additional modality 引入的 slightly higher token heterogeneity。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'CV=0.219 完成 6-model spectrum：π0(0.038) < π0.5(0.055) < X-VLA(0.151) <\n    OpenVLA(0.215) ≈ OFT(0.219) < SmolVLA(0.314)。 Paper Table 1 中 OFT 行填入 CV=0.219,\n    Entropy=0.667, Pruning=''Graded (predicted)''。\n\n    '\n- name: X-VLA k=0.8/k=0.85 3-Seed Cliff Localization\n  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n  description: 'X-VLA Object cliff threshold 精确定位：k=0.85 (67.9% ± 0.31pp, 3-seed)\n    和 k=0.80 (89.0% ± 0.72pp, 3-seed)。Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    xvla_l2norm_k085_object_mean: 67.9\n    xvla_l2norm_k085_object_std: 0.31\n    xvla_l2norm_k085_seeds:\n    - 68.0\n    - 67.6\n    - 68.2\n    xvla_l2norm_k080_object_mean: 89.0\n    xvla_l2norm_k080_object_std: 0.72\n    xvla_l2norm_k080_seeds:\n    - 88.8\n    - 88.4\n    - 89.8\n    xvla_random_k085_object_mean: 64.3\n    xvla_random_k085_seeds:\n    - 65.0\n    - 63.6\n    - 63.2\n    xvla_random_k080_object_mean: 89.4\n    xvla_random_k080_seeds:\n    - 89.4\n    non_monotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n    cliff_width_k_units: 0.05\n    l2norm_random_k085_gap_pp: 3.6\n    both_crash_same_tasks: true\n  result_rationale: \"3-seed deterministic data 确认 cliff 位于 k=0.85（42 tokens kept），且\\\n    \\ k=0.80（40 tokens）recovery 到 89%——仅差 2 个 tokens 但 21pp gap。\\nNon-monotonicity\\\n    \\ 来自 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interactions： - k=0.85 (42 tokens): BART\\\n    \\ 的 12-layer self-attention 在 42 tokens 上产生\\n  destructive interference pattern——刚好是\\\n    \\ critical token density threshold\\n- k=0.80 (40 tokens): 少保留 2 个 tokens 反而破坏了这个\\\n    \\ interference pattern，\\n  恢复了正常的 information flow\\n\\nSD < 1pp across all 3 seeds\\\n    \\ 确认 cliff 是完全 deterministic 的（L2norm pruning 是 deterministic function of token\\\n    \\ norms），不是 stochastic noise。\\nL2norm 和 random 在 cliff zone 都 crash on same 4\\\n    \\ tasks (T1=cream_cheese, T4=ketchup, T6=butter, T8=chocolate_pudding) → cliff\\\n    \\ 是 architectural， 不是 method-specific。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - caption: X-VLA Object Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic (L2norm)\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Tokens Kept\n    - Seed 42\n    - Seed 43\n    - Seed 44\n    - Mean\n    - SD\n    rows:\n    - - '0.90'\n      - '45'\n      - 97.6%\n      - —\n      - 98.2%\n      - 97.6%\n      - —\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '42'\n      - 68.0%\n      - 67.6%\n      - 68.2%\n      - 67.9%\n      - '0.31'\n    - - '0.80'\n      - '40'\n      - 88.8%\n      - 88.4%\n      - 89.8%\n      - 89.0%\n      - '0.72'\n    - - '0.70'\n      - '35'\n      - 56.2%\n      - 59.0%\n      - 56.4%\n      - 57.2%\n      - '1.56'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: X-VLA Object cliff profile with 3-seed error bars — sharp V-shape at k=0.85,\n    recovery at k=0.80. Annotate ''2 tokens, 21pp gap''.'\n  analysis: 'Cliff localization 完成。Paper 中用 1 figure 展示 X-VLA 的 full pruning curve\n    (k=0.1 to k=0.95)，annotate k=0.85 cliff 和 non-monotonic recovery。 Discussion 中说明\n    BART encoder 的 length-dependent interaction 机制。\n\n    '\n- name: RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler Fine-tune + Pruning\n  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n  description: 'Perceiver Resampler connector 作为第 3 个 connector family 验证。 Training\n    killed twice。Median tier 预测即使完成也不会改变核心结论。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    training_status: killed\n    training_attempts: 2\n    roboflamingo_predicted_cv: 0.18\n    roboflamingo_predicted_entropy: 0.72\n    roboflamingo_predicted_baseline_sr: 55\n    roboflamingo_predicted_k09_sr: 48\n    roboflamingo_predicted_k05_sr: 28\n    would_strengthen_paper: false\n    paper_coverage_without: 5 models × 3 families sufficient for CoRL\n  result_rationale: 'RoboFlamingo training 两次 killed，likely due to (1) Perceiver Resampler\n    与 LIBERO task distribution 的 incompatibility，(2) fine-tuning instability from\n    frozen cross-attention + trainable resampler 的 gradient mismatch。\n\n    即使完成，Perceiver Resampler 的预测 CV=0.18 会落在 X-VLA 和 OpenVLA 之间—— 介于 token-entangling\n    和 token-independent 之间。这不会改变 2-axis framework 的核心结论，只是增加一个中间数据点。\n\n    Median tier 下 5 models × 3 families (linear / MLP / pixel-shuffle) 已经足够 支撑 CoRL\n    submission。Perceiver Resampler 作为 ''future work'' 提及。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Dropped from paper scope。在 Discussion 中提到 ''additional connector families\n    (e.g., Perceiver Resampler, cross-attention based) remain to be validated'' 作为\n    limitation 和 future direction。\n\n    '\n- name: E5 Attention-Based Pruning — X-VLA vs π0.5 Cross-Suite\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: 'Attention-based pruning (E5) 在 X-VLA 和 π0.5 上的 cross-suite 结果。 X-VLA\n    attention pruning 表现极好（Object 99.2%, Long 90.2%）， π0.5 attention 在 Object k=0.7\n    catastrophic (0.6%) 但 Goal 70.2%。 Median tier：Goal 初始 0% 后修复为 98.2%，需额外 seed 确认可靠性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    xvla_attn_last_k05_object: 99.2\n    xvla_attn_mean_k05_object: 98.4\n    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_object: 97.4\n    xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial: 88.8\n    xvla_attn_mean_k05_spatial: 91.6\n    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_spatial: 92.8\n    xvla_attn_last_k05_goal: 98.2\n    xvla_attn_mean_k05_goal: 97.4\n    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_goal: 96.8\n    xvla_attn_last_k05_long: 90.2\n    xvla_attn_mean_k05_long: 94.0\n    xvla_attn_rollout_k05_long: 94.8\n    xvla_attn_last_k03_object: 84.2\n    xvla_attn_mean_k03_object: 96.0\n    xvla_attn_mean_k03_spatial: 90.4\n    xvla_attn_last_k03_spatial: 85.6\n    pi05_attn_k095_object: 98.4\n    pi05_attn_k09_object: 97.2\n    pi05_attn_k085_object: 92.2\n    pi05_attn_k07_object: 0.6\n    pi05_attn_k05_object: 37.8\n    pi05_attn_k05_spatial: 72.6\n    pi05_attn_k05_goal: 71.2\n    pi05_attn_k05_long: 49.4\n    openvla_attn_k09_object: 61.4\n    openvla_attn_k085_object: 55.0\n    openvla_attn_k09_goal: 73.2\n    openvla_attn_k09_spatial: 80.4\n    xvla_attn_goal_fix_needed: true\n    xvla_attn_goal_seed42_sr: 98.2\n    xvla_attn_goal_seed43_needed: true\n    xvla_attn_goal_predicted_seed43_sr: 97.5\n  result_rationale: 'E5 attention pruning 在不同 model 上表现 divergent：\n\n    X-VLA (BART encoder)：attention pruning 近乎 lossless，因为 BART 的 12-layer self-attention\n    产生了 meaningful attention patterns——high-attention tokens 确实 是最重要的。k=0.5 Object\n    99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → attention 比 L2norm 好 56.6pp。 这是因为 BART encoder 的 attention\n    直接反映了 token 间的 functional dependency。\n\n    Goal suite 初始为 0%（bug），修复后 98.2% → 需要 seed43 确认 fix 是 genuine。 Median tier 预测\n    seed43 = 97.5%（fix 是 valid 的，但需要额外 seed 才能在 paper 中 claim）。\n\n    π0.5 (linear projection)：attention pruning 在 k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%)， 因为 PaliGemma\n    的 per-layer attention 在中间 k 值产生了 adversarial selection。 π0.5 的 attention entropy\n    = 0.666，说明 attention 分布有 moderate sharpness， 但不 correlate with true token importance（CV=0.055\n    说明所有 tokens equally important）。Attention-based pruning 在 uniform-importance model\n    上不可靠。\n\n    OpenVLA (MLP)：attention pruning k=0.9 Object = 61.4% < L2norm = 70.6% < random\n    = 69.2%。 Attention 是三种方法中最差的，因为 MLP connector 后的 attention 也不 reliable predict\n    token importance。\n\n    Paper value：attention pruning 的 effectiveness 也是 connector-dependent， strengthening\n    ''connector determines optimal compression strategy'' claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: E5 Attention Pruning k=0.5 — Cross-Model Cross-Suite\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    rows:\n    - - X-VLA (attn-last)\n      - 99.2%\n      - 88.8%\n      - 98.2%*\n      - 90.2%\n    - - X-VLA (attn-mean)\n      - 98.4%\n      - 91.6%\n      - 97.4%\n      - 94.0%\n    - - pi0.5 (attn)\n      - 37.8%\n      - 72.6%\n      - 71.2%\n      - 49.4%\n    - - X-VLA (L2norm)\n      - 42.6%\n      - 58.8%\n      - 59.0%\n      - 44.6%\n    - - X-VLA (random)\n      - 70.6%\n      - 71.4%\n      - 67.9%\n      - 61.6%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Method comparison radar chart — X-VLA at k=0.5: attention (near-lossless)\n    vs L2norm (42.6%) vs random (70.6%) across 4 suites. Shows attention dominance\n    for BART connector.'\n  analysis: 'E5 attention pruning 提供了 Claim 5 的重要扩展：不只是 L2norm vs random 的 strategy\n    depends on CV，attention-based methods 也是 connector-dependent。 BART connector 的\n    attention 是 reliable signal（因为 12-layer self-attention creates meaningful importance\n    distribution），而 linear/MLP connector 的 attention 不可靠。Paper 中可以加一行 Table showing\n    method effectiveness rank per model。 但 Goal 0%→98.2% 的 fix 需要 seed43 确认，Median\n    tier 下这个 reliability concern 需要在 paper 中 transparent disclosure。\n\n    '\n- name: CV Scaling Law — Spearman Correlation Across Conditions\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: 'CV 作为 pruning strategy predictor 的 Spearman correlation 分析。 Median\n    tier 预测 abs(Spearman) 在 0.6-0.85 之间。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spearman: 0.82\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_p_value: 0.03\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_spearman: 0.75\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_p_value: 0.05\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spearman: 0.45\n    cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_p_value: 0.15\n    cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.74\n    n_models_k05: 3\n    n_suites_k05: 1\n    datapoints_k05:\n    - model: pi0.5\n      cv: 0.055\n      gap_pp: -35.4\n    - model: X-VLA\n      cv: 0.151\n      gap_pp: -26.9\n    - model: OpenVLA\n      cv: 0.215\n      gap_pp: 1.8\n    k05_gap_monotonic: true\n    k07_gap_monotonic: true\n    k03_gap_monotonic: false\n  result_rationale: 'CV scaling law 的 Spearman correlation 0.74 落在 median tier range\n    [0.6, 0.85] 中。\n\n    k=0.5 是最 clean 的 scaling law validation point：3 个 model 的 L2norm-random gap 与\n    CV 呈单调关系（-35.4pp → -26.9pp → +1.8pp as CV increases 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215）。 Spearman\n    = 0.82，因为只有 3 个 data points 所以 p-value 边缘显著。\n\n    k=0.7 作为 confirmatory second row：pattern 一致但 gap magnitudes 小（-22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4），\n    Spearman = 0.75。\n\n    k=0.3 BREAKS the scaling law：π0.5 reversal (+18.9pp L2norm wins) 但 X-VLA random\n    仍大幅领先 (+42.3pp)。这不是 CV 不好，而是 absolute token budget 的交互效应： π0.5 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（大\n    budget），X-VLA k=0.3 保留 15 tokens（小 budget）。 Large budget + low CV = L2norm 可以\n    fragment clusters 恢复 diversity。 Small budget + mid CV = 无论如何都太少，random 保持 stochastic\n    diversity 的优势。\n\n    Paper strategy：k=0.5 作为 main table，k=0.7 作为 confirmatory。k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion\n    中说明，强调 ''CV predicts strategy preference at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7);\n    at extreme compression (k=0.3), absolute token budget introduces additional interaction''。Claim\n    5 加限定 ''at moderate compression''。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: CV Scaling Law — L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) at k=0.5 and k=0.7\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Gap k=0.7 (pp)\n    - Gap k=0.5 (pp)\n    - Gap k=0.3 (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - pi0.5\n      - '0.055'\n      - '-22.2'\n      - '-35.4'\n      - '+18.9'\n    - - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - '-6.5'\n      - '-26.9'\n      - '-42.3'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - '+5.4'\n      - '+1.8'\n      - '+3.6'\n  - caption: 'Spearman Correlation: CV vs Strategy Gap'\n    columns:\n    - k value\n    - Spearman rho\n    - p-value\n    - Monotonic?\n    rows:\n    - - '0.7'\n      - '0.75'\n      - '0.05'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - '0.5'\n      - '0.82'\n      - '0.03'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - '0.3'\n      - '0.45'\n      - '0.15'\n      - No (reversal)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Scatter plot with regression line — CV (x-axis) vs L2norm-Random gap (y-axis)\n    at k=0.5. Three points with clear positive trend. Annotate Spearman=0.82.'\n  analysis: 'Claim 5 survives review but需要加限定。原 claim ''CV predicts optimal pruning\n    strategy'' 改为 ''CV predicts optimal pruning strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)''。\n    k=0.3 reversal 说明 strategy preference = f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget)， 不是仅 CV\n    决定。这个 nuance 在 median tier 下是可以接受的——reviewers 会 appreciate honest boundary conditions。3-4\n    个 claims survive review 的预测中，这个 claim 以 qualified form survive。\n\n    '\n- name: SmolVLA VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Consolidation + Architecture Control\n  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n  description: 'VTR M-sweep (M=16/32/64/96/128) 的 3-seed 最终结果 + MLP adapter 对照。 已有大量数据，Median\n    tier 下 consolidate 最终 statistics。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    vtr_m16_3seed_mean: 56.9\n    vtr_m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n    vtr_m16_3seed_seeds:\n    - 55.8\n    - 58.4\n    - 56.5\n    vtr_m32_3seed_mean: 60.1\n    vtr_m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n    vtr_m32_3seed_seeds:\n    - 61.6\n    - 59.2\n    - 59.6\n    vtr_m64_3seed_mean: 62.0\n    vtr_m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n    vtr_m64_3seed_seeds:\n    - 61.6\n    - 60.0\n    - 64.4\n    vtr_m96_3seed_mean: 54.5\n    vtr_m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n    vtr_m96_3seed_seeds:\n    - 52.6\n    - 58.2\n    - 52.8\n    vtr_m128_3seed_mean: 58.0\n    vtr_m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n    vtr_m128_3seed_seeds:\n    - 59.8\n    - 54.0\n    - 60.2\n    m_curve_range_pp: 7.5\n    m_curve_vs_baseline_max_diff: 5.3\n    m_curve_flat: true\n    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean: 63.4\n    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std: 2.6\n    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_seeds:\n    - 65.2\n    - 64.6\n    - 60.4\n    vtc_vs_mlp_t_stat: 1.94\n    vtc_vs_mlp_p_value: 0.15\n    architecture_independent: true\n    smolvla_baseline: 59.2\n    hard_prune_k05: 0\n    recovery_from_zero: true\n  result_rationale: 'VTR M-sweep 确认 M-curve 是 flat 的：M=16 (56.9%) 到 M=128 (58.0%)，\n    all within ±5pp of baseline 59.2%。这意味着 VTR 对 pixel-shuffle connector 实现了 near-lossless\n    compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%)。\n\n    M=64 是 absolute best (62.0%)，M=96 是 lowest (54.5%) 但 p=0.034 与 M=64 的差异 statistically\n    significant——M=96 的 higher variance (3.2pp) 和 lower mean 可能是因为 96-token representation\n    落在 an awkward regime：不够多以 passthrough (M=128)，但 compression ratio 不够大 to force\n    useful abstraction (M=32/64)。\n\n    MLP adapter (63.4%) vs VTC (60.1%) p=0.15 → architecture independent。 任何 learned\n    re-encoding 都能从 0% 恢复到 baseline。\n\n    Median tier 下 VTR 的 contribution statement 明确：''VTR achieves near-lossless compression\n    at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors, recovering from 0% (hard pruning) to\n    ~59% (baseline)''。不 overclaim 超过 baseline。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: VTR M-Sweep — 3-Seed Statistics (SmolVLA Object)\n    columns:\n    - M\n    - Compression\n    - Mean SR (%)\n    - Std (pp)\n    - vs Baseline\n    rows:\n    - - '16'\n      - 87.5%\n      - '56.9'\n      - '1.3'\n      - -2.3pp\n    - - '32'\n      - 75.0%\n      - '60.1'\n      - '1.3'\n      - +0.9pp\n    - - '64'\n      - 50.0%\n      - '62.0'\n      - '2.3'\n      - +2.8pp\n    - - '96'\n      - 25.0%\n      - '54.5'\n      - '3.2'\n      - -4.7pp\n    - - '128'\n      - 0% (pass)\n      - '58.0'\n      - '3.5'\n      - -1.2pp\n    - - MLP-32\n      - 75.0%\n      - '63.4'\n      - '2.6'\n      - +4.2pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: M-curve with error bars — flat profile, all within baseline ±5pp band (shaded).\n    Hard prune reference at 0%.'\n  analysis: 'VTR results 完备。Paper 中用 M-curve figure + architecture control table 支撑\n    Claim 4。Key limitation：仅对 pixel-shuffle 有效（OpenVLA 0%）， method contribution 限于\n    worst-case architecture。\n\n    '\n- name: Claims Survival Under Review — Median Tier Assessment\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: '5 个 core claims 在 median tier 下的 review survival 预测。 预测 3-4 个 claims\n    survive。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    claims_surviving: 3.5\n    claim_1_2axis_framework:\n      status: survives with qualification\n      original: governed by two axes\n      revised: primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity\n        as a modulating factor for token-entangling connectors\n      qualification: Axis-2 amplification weak for token-independent connectors (π0.5)\n      strength: 0.8\n    claim_2_pixel_shuffle_entanglement:\n      status: survives fully\n      evidence: 7 conditions × 4 suites × official checkpoint → 0%\n      strength: 1.0\n    claim_3_graded_degradation:\n      status: survives fully\n      evidence: OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT CV/entropy confirmation\n      strength: 0.95\n    claim_4_vtr_recovery:\n      status: survives with limitation\n      original: universal compression via VTR\n      revised: VTR recovers pixel-shuffle from 0% to baseline; ineffective for MLP\n        projector\n      limitation: method contribution narrowed to pixel-shuffle-specific\n      strength: 0.7\n    claim_5_cv_scaling_law:\n      status: survives with boundary condition\n      original: CV predicts optimal strategy\n      revised: CV predicts optimal strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)\n      boundary: k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models with large token budgets\n      strength: 0.75\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 预测 3.5 claims survive（3 full + 1.5 qualified），落在\n    [3, 4] range。\n\n    Claim 2（pixel-shuffle entanglement）是最 robust 的——0% at k=0.95, all methods, all\n    suites, official checkpoint, dual-seed confirmed。没有任何 edge case。\n\n    Claim 3（graded degradation）也 robust——OpenVLA 6-point curve 是 clean monotonic，\n    OFT CV/entropy confirmation 是 clean controlled comparison。\n\n    Claim 1（2-axis framework）需要 qualification 因为 Axis-2 对 token-independent connectors\n    的 amplification 弱于预期。Paper 不能说 ''task complexity always amplifies pruning sensitivity''，而是\n    ''task complexity amplifies sensitivity SPECIFICALLY for token-entangling connectors\n    where pruning damage cascades''。\n\n    Claim 4（VTR）的 method contribution 收窄——OpenVLA 0% 意味着 VTR 不是 universal。 Reviewers\n    可能 question: ''if VTR only works on pixel-shuffle, and pixel-shuffle is the architecture\n    you''re warning against, isn''t the method contribution circular?'' Response:\n    ''VTR provides a migration path for existing pixel-shuffle VLAs, not a design\n    recommendation for new ones.''\n\n    Claim 5（CV scaling law）加 boundary condition 后仍有价值——k=0.5-0.7 的 scaling law 是 clean\n    的（Spearman 0.75-0.82），只是 k=0.3 有 reversal。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Claims Survival Assessment — Median Tier\n    columns:\n    - Claim\n    - Original Strength\n    - Median Tier Status\n    - Revised Strength\n    rows:\n    - - 'C1: 2-Axis Framework'\n      - Strong\n      - Qualified\n      - '0.80'\n    - - 'C2: Pixel-Shuffle'\n      - Strong\n      - Fully Survives\n      - '1.00'\n    - - 'C3: Graded Degradation'\n      - Strong\n      - Fully Survives\n      - '0.95'\n    - - 'C4: VTR Recovery'\n      - Moderate\n      - Limited to pixel-shuffle\n      - '0.70'\n    - - 'C5: CV Scaling Law'\n      - Moderate\n      - Boundary at k=0.3\n      - '0.75'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Paper identity 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method'。 Title 改为\n    'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'—— 更保守但准确。Contribution\n    statement 聚焦：(1) first systematic cross-architecture token pruning analysis in\n    VLAs (5 models × 4 suites), (2) CV as zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance\n    AND strategy, (3) VTR as targeted recovery method for worst-case (pixel-shuffle)\n    connectors。仍提交 CoRL。\n","numLines":1143,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1143}}}
