{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RZXgbEiLVBaDVsbFrET2k1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024\"},{\"title\":\"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up\",\"url\":\"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"}]\n\nI found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nThe paper can be desk rejected for one of the three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope.\n\n## Scope Requirements\n\nAll CoRL submissions must demonstrate the relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots OR testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search result shows information about the review criteria and desk rejection process, but the page content appears to be truncated. For the complete scoring scale and detailed rating criteria, you may want to visit the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews to see all the evaluation guidelines and any numerical scoring scales that might be used for paper reviews.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f75ff7-cbcf-4297-8f4a-a59d253e665c","uuid":"d0882e09-59e3-4565-acb4-c02765d48079","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:09:39.529Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Vc1ZZViChL7iNgjuXgFH52","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery","url":"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024"},{"title":"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up","url":"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"}]},"I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nThe paper can be desk rejected for one of the three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope.\n\n## Scope Requirements\n\nAll CoRL submissions must demonstrate the relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots OR testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search result shows information about the review criteria and desk rejection process, but the page content appears to be truncated. For the complete scoring scale and detailed rating criteria, you may want to visit the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews to see all the evaluation guidelines and any numerical scoring scales that might be used for paper reviews."],"durationSeconds":5.723894173000001}}
