{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CZdELwj7i1DMxZfZRvt5uL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've gathered enough information about CoRL. Let me compile what I know:\n\n- CoRL uses OpenReview\n- CoRL 2024 had 671 submissions\n- CoRL typically uses a 1-10 rating scale (standard for ML conferences on OpenReview)\n- Acceptance rate is typically around 30-35% for CoRL based on historical data\n- Review dimensions include: significance, novelty, quality, clarity, relevance to robot learning\n\nFor the review form, I'll use the standard CoRL/OpenReview format which typically includes:\n- Overall Score: 1-10 scale\n- Confidence: 1-5\n\n\n- Soundness, Presentation, Contribution, and Overall assessment\n\nNow I have everything I need to proceed: the paper, the review context with imagined experiments, and CoRL venue details. I'll dispatch two reviewers in parallel—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—then conduct a full roundtable discussion through all four steps.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3097,"cache_read_input_tokens":69286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3097},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3f75ff7-cbcf-4297-8f4a-a59d253e665c","uuid":"dd1b0677-127a-409f-8d4b-8be0a87d41ed"}
